コードの設定手順を提供し、Python開発ガイドラインとAIエージェントを使用する方法を説明します","ko":"본 가이드라인은 클라우드 코드 설정 단계를 제공하며 파이썬 개발 가이드라인 및 AI 에이전트를 사용하는 방법을 설명합니다","es":"Configuración de Claude Code para desarrolladores de Python. Guías y recursos para empezar a trabajar con agentes de IA","fr":"Configuration de Claude Code pour les développeurs Python. Guides et ressources pour commencer à travailler avec des outils d''IA","de":"Konfiguration von Claude Code für Python-Entwickler. Anleitungen und Ressourcen, um mit KI-Agents zu beginnen","pt":"Configuração do código Claude para desenvolvimento Python. Aprenda a criar soluções de IA com facilidade.","ru":"Настройка кода Claude для разработки на Python. Создавайте решения ИИ с легкостью.","ar":"تكوين رمز كلود لتحقيق تطوير پایتون. تعلم كيفية إنشاء حلول ذكاء اصطناعي بسهولة.","en":"Setup for claude code"},"definition":{"en":"Setup for claude code"},"features":{"zh":["设置Claude代码的步骤","使用Python开发指南","AI智能开发工具的集成","提高开发效率","简化代码设置过程"],"ja":["Claudeコードの設定手順","Python開発ガイドラインの使用","AIエージェントの統合","開発効率の向上","コード設定プロセスの簡素化"],"ko":["클라우드 코드 설정 단계","파이썬 개발 가이드라인 사용","AI 에이전트 통합","개발 효율성 향상","코드 설정 프로세스 간소화"],"es":["Configuración de Claude Code","Desarrollo de aplicaciones de Python con agentes de IA","Uso de herramientas de IA para automatizar tareas","Guías y recursos para desarrolladores de Python","Integración con otros frameworks y bibliotecas de Python"],"fr":["Configuration de Claude Code","Développement d''applications Python avec des outils d''IA","Utilisation d''outils d''IA pour automatiser des tâches","Guides et ressources pour les développeurs Python","Intégration avec d''autres frameworks et bibliothèques Python"],"de":["Konfiguration von Claude Code","Entwicklung von Python-Anwendungen mit KI-Agents","Verwendung von KI-Tools zur Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Anleitungen und Ressourcen für Python-Entwickler","Integration mit anderen Frameworks und Bibliotheken von Python"],"pt":["Configuração do código Claude","Desenvolvimento de soluções de IA","Uso de bibliotecas Python","Criação de modelos de machine learning","Integração com outras tecnologias"],"ru":["Настройка кода Claude","Разработка решений ИИ","Использование библиотек Python","Создание моделей машинного обучения","Интеграция с другими технологиями"],"ar":["تكوين رمز كلود","تطوير حلول ذكاء اصطناعي","استخدام مكتبات پایتون","إنشاء نماذج من تعلم الآلة","التكامل مع تكنولوجيا أخرى"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python开发指南","AI智能开发工具","Claude代码设置","开发效率提高","代码设置简化","如何使用Python开发指南","AIエージェント的替代品","Python开发指南安装"],"ja":["Python開発ガイドライン","AIエージェント","Claudeコード設定","開発効率向上","コード設定簡素化","Python開発ガイドラインの使用方法","AIエージェントの代替","Python開発ガイドラインのインストール"],"ko":["파이썬 개발 가이드라인","AI 에이전트","클라우드 코드 설정","개발 효율성 향상","코드 설정 간소화","파이썬 개발 가이드라인 사용 방법","AI 에이전트의 대체","파이썬 개발 가이드라인 설치"],"es":["cómo usar agentes de IA","guías de desarrollo de Python","herramientas de IA para Python","configuración de Claude Code","desarrollo de aplicaciones de Python con agentes de IA","alternativas a Claude Code","instalación de Claude Code"],"fr":["comment utiliser les outils d''IA","guides de développement Python","outils d''IA pour Python","configuration de Claude Code","développement d''applications Python avec des outils d''IA","alternatives à Claude Code","installation de Claude Code"],"de":["wie man KI-Agents verwendet","Entwicklungsrichtlinien für Python","KI-Tools für Python","Konfiguration von Claude Code","Entwicklung von Python-Anwendungen mit KI-Agents","Alternativen zu Claude Code","Installation von Claude Code"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de ia","o que é ia","ferramentas de ia alternative","ia vs machine learning","instalar ferramentas de ia","guia de desenvolvimento python","desenvolvimento de soluções de ia","bibliotecas python para ia"],"ru":["как использовать ии агенты","что такое ии","ии агенты alternative","ии vs машинное обучение","установить ии агенты","руководство по разработке на python","разработка решений ии","библиотеки python для ии"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هي أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي بديلة","الذكاء الاصطناعي مقابل تعلم الآلة","تثبيت أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","دليل تطوير پایتون","تطوير حلول ذكاء اصطناعي","مكتبات پایتون لأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"NmBoyd","repo":"claude_setup","repoPath":"NmBoyd/claude_setup","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.915Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-dev-guidelines","description":"Python development guidelines for modern Python projects. Use when creating Python modules, classes, functions, scripts, or working with type hints, pytest, packaging (pip/poetry), virtual environments, async/await, data classes, or Python best practices. Covers project structure, typing, testing patterns, error handling, logging, and Pythonic idioms.","bodyPreview":"# Python Development Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nEstablish consistency and best practices for Python development, covering modern Python 3.12+ patterns, type safety, testing, and project organization.\n\n---\n\n## Standards Overview\n\n| Category | Standard |\n|----------|----------|\n| **Python** | 3.12+, FastAPI, async/await preferred |\n| **Formatting** | ruff (96-char lines, double quotes, sorted imports) |\n| **Typing** | Strict (Pydantic v2 models preferred); `from __future__ import annotations` |\n| **N","body":"# Python Development Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nEstablish consistency and best practices for Python development, covering modern Python 3.12+ patterns, type safety, testing, and project organization.\n\n---\n\n## Standards Overview\n\n| Category | Standard |\n|----------|----------|\n| **Python** | 3.12+, FastAPI, async/await preferred |\n| **Formatting** | ruff (96-char lines, double quotes, sorted imports) |\n| **Typing** | Strict (Pydantic v2 models preferred); `from __future__ import annotations` |\n| **Naming** | `snake_case` (functions/variables), `PascalCase` (classes), `SCREAMING_SNAKE` (constants) |\n| **Error Handling** | Typed exceptions; context managers for resources |\n| **Documentation** | Google-style docstrings for public functions/classes |\n| **Testing** | Separate test files matching source file patterns |\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nAutomatically activates when working on:\n- Creating or modifying Python files (`.py`)\n- Writing classes, functions, or modules\n- Setting up Python projects (pyproject.toml, setup.py)\n- Writing tests with pytest\n- Working with type hints and mypy\n- Async/await patterns with FastAPI\n- Package management (pip, poetry, conda)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### New Python Project Checklist\n\n- [ ] **Python version**: 3.12+ specified in `.python-version`\n- [ ] **Project structure**: src layout or flat layout\n- [ ] **pyproject.toml**: Modern packaging config with ruff\n- [ ] **Type hints**: Strict typing with `from __future__ import annotations`\n- [ ] **Tests**: pytest with fixtures, matching source patterns\n- [ ] **Linting**: ruff (96-char lines, double quotes, sorted imports)\n- [ ] **Virtual env**: venv, poetry, or conda\n- [ ] **Documentation**: Google-style docstrings\n- [ ] **Exceptions**: Hierarchical exceptions in `exceptions.py`\n\n### New Module Checklist\n\n- [ ] `from __future__ import annotations` at top\n- [ ] Module docstring (Google-style)\n- [ ] Type hints on all public functions\n- [ ] `__all__` export list (if applicable)\n- [ ] Unit tests in `tests/` mirror structure\n- [ ] Error handling with typed exceptions from `exceptions.py`\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n### Recommended Layout (src-layout)\n\n```\nproject/\n├── src/\n│   └── mypackage/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── exceptions.py     # Hierarchical typed exceptions\n│       ├── core/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   └── module.py\n│       ├── utils/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   └── helpers.py\n│       └── py.typed          # PEP 561 marker\n├── tests/\n│   ├── conftest.py           # Shared fixtures\n│   ├── test_core/\n│   │   └── test_module.py    # Mirrors src/mypackage/core/module.py\n│   └── test_utils/\n│       └── test_helpers.py   # Mirrors src/mypackage/utils/helpers.py\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── ruff.toml                 # ruff config (96-char, double quotes)\n├── README.md\n└── .python-version           # 3.12+\n```\n\n### Alternative: Flat Layout (smaller projects)\n\n```\nproject/\n├── mypackage/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   └── module.py\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_module.py\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles (7 Key Rules)\n\n### 1. Type Everything Public (Strict Typing)\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations  # Always at top of file\n\n# ❌ NEVER: Untyped public functions\ndef process_data(data):\n    return data.upper()\n\n# ✅ ALWAYS: Full type annotations\ndef process_data(data: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Process input data.\n\n    Args:\n        data: The input string to process.\n\n    Returns:\n        The processed uppercase string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return data.upper()\n```\n\n### 2. Use Pydantic v2 for Data Models (Preferred)\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, EmailStr, Field\n\n# ✅ Pydantic v2 for validation (preferred)\nclass UserCreate(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"User creation model with validation.\"\"\"\n\n    name: str = Field(..., min_length=1, max_length=100)\n    email: EmailStr\n\nclass UserResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"User response model.\"\"\"\n\n    id: int\n    name: str\n    email: str\n\n# For simple internal data without validation, dataclasses are acceptable\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass InternalConfig:\n    timeout: int = 30\n    retries: int = 3\n```\n\n### 3. Handle Errors with Typed Hierarchical Exceptions\n\n```python\n# exceptions.py - Define hierarchical typed exceptions\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n\nclass AppError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for application errors.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(message)\n\n\nclass ValidationError(AppError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when validation fails.\"\"\"\n\n    pass\n\n\nclass NotFoundError(AppError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when resource not found.\"\"\"\n\n    pass\n\n\nclass DatabaseError(AppError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when database operation fails.\"\"\"\n\n    pass\n\n\n# Usage - catch specific exceptions, not general Exception\nfrom mypackage.exceptions import ValidationError, NotFoundError\n\nasync def get_user(user_id: int) -> User:\n    \"\"\"Get user by ID.\n\n    Args:\n        user_id: The user''s unique identifier.\n\n    Returns:\n        The user object.\n\n    Raises:\n        NotFoundError: If user does not exist.\n    \"\"\"\n    user = await db.find(user_id)\n    if not user:\n        raise NotFoundError(f\"User {user_id} not found\")\n    return user\n```\n\n### 4. Use Context Managers for Resources\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager, contextmanager\n\n# ❌ NEVER: Manual resource management\nf = open(\"file.txt\")\ndata = f.read()\nf.close()\n\n# ✅ ALWAYS: Context managers\nwith open(\"file.txt\") as f:\n    data = f.read()\n\n# ✅ Sync context manager\n@contextmanager\ndef database_transaction():\n    \"\"\"Manage database transaction with automatic cleanup.\"\"\"\n    conn = get_connection()\n    try:\n        yield conn\n        conn.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        conn.rollback()\n        raise\n    finally:\n        conn.close()\n\n# ✅ Async - use try/finally to ensure cleanup\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def async_db_session():\n    \"\"\"Manage async database session with cleanup.\"\"\"\n    session = await create_session()\n    try:\n        yield session\n        await session.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        await session.rollback()\n        raise\n    finally:\n        await session.close()\n```\n\n### 5. Prefer Composition Over Inheritance\n\n```python\n# ❌ Avoid deep inheritance\nclass Animal: ...\nclass Mammal(Animal): ...\nclass Dog(Mammal): ...\n\n# ✅ Prefer composition and protocols\nfrom typing import Protocol\n\nclass Walker(Protocol):\n    def walk(self) -> None: ...\n\nclass Dog:\n    def __init__(self, legs: int = 4):\n        self.legs = legs\n\n    def walk(self) -> None:\n        print(f\"Walking on {self.legs} legs\")\n```\n\n### 6. Use Logging, Not Print\n\n```python\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# ❌ NEVER\nprint(f\"Processing {item}\")\n\n# ✅ ALWAYS\nlogger.info(\"Processing %s\", item)\nlogger.error(\"Failed to process\", exc_info=True)\n```\n\n### 7. Write Testable Code\n\n```python\n# ❌ Hard to test: hidden dependencies\ndef send_email(user_id: int) -> None:\n    user = database.get_user(user_id)  # Hidden dependency\n    smtp.send(user.email, \"Hello\")      # Hidden dependency\n\n# ✅ Easy to test: explicit dependencies\ndef send_email(\n    user: User,\n    email_sender: EmailSender\n) -> None:\n    email_sender.send(user.email, \"Hello\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Type Hints Quick Reference\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom typing import TypeVar, Generic\nfrom collections.abc import Callable\n\n# Basic types (Python 3.12+)\nvalues: list[int] = [1, 2, 3]\nmapping: dict[str, int] = {\"a\": 1}\nvalue: str | None = None  # Union syntax\n\n# Callable and Generics\nhandler: Callable[[int, str], bool]\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\n\nclass Container(Generic[T]):\n    def __init__(self, value: T) -> None:\n        self.value = value\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Patterns\n\n```python\n# tests/test_user_service.py - mirrors src/mypackage/services/user_service.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport pytest\nfrom mypackage.services import UserService\nfrom mypackage.exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass TestUserService:\n    \"\"\"Tests for UserService.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_create_user_success(self, mock_database):\n        \"\"\"Should create user with valid data.\"\"\"\n        service = UserService(mock_database)\n        user = service.create(name=\"Test\", email=\"test@example.com\")\n        assert user.name == \"Test\"\n\n    def test_create_user_invalid_email_raises(self, mock_database):\n        \"\"\"Should raise ValidationError for invalid email.\"\"\"\n        service = UserService(mock_database)\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\"invalid email\"):\n            service.create(name=\"Test\", email=\"not-an-email\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n❌ Mutable default arguments (`def foo(items=[])`)\n❌ Bare `except:` clauses - catch specific exceptions\n❌ Catching general `Exception` - use typed exceptions\n❌ `from module import *`\n❌ Global mutable state\n❌ Ignoring type checker errors\n❌ print() instead of logging\n❌ String concatenation in loops (use join)\n❌ Not using `if __name__ == \"__main__\":`\n❌ Missing `from __future__ import annotations`\n\n---\n\n## Async Patterns (FastAPI Preferred)\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status\nfrom mypackage.exceptions import ValidationError\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# ✅ FastAPI endpoint with proper error handling\n@app.post(\"/users\", response_model=UserResponse, status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)\nasync def create_user(user: UserCreate) -> UserResponse:\n    \"\"\"Create a new user.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return await user_service.create(user)\n    except ValidationError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e)) from e\n\n# ✅ Async error handling with exception chaining (from e)\nasync def process_data(data: dict) -> Result:\n    \"\"\"Process data with proper exception handling.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return await do_processing(data)\n    except KeyError as e:\n        raise ValidationError(f\"Missing required field: {e}\") from e\n\n# ✅ Concurrent operations\nasync def process_items(items: list[str]) -> list[dict]:\n    return await asyncio.gather(*[fetch_data(item) for item in items])\n```\n\n---\n\n## Resource Files\n\n### [style-guide.md](resources/style-guide.md)\nGoogle Python Style Guide + PEP 8 practices, naming, docstrings, imports\n\n<!-- ### [project-setup.md](resources/project-setup.md)\npyproject.toml, poetry, pip, virtual environments\n\n### [typing-guide.md](resources/typing-guide.md)\nAdvanced type hints, generics, protocols, mypy configuration\n\n### [testing-patterns.md](resources/testing-patterns.md)\npytest fixtures, mocking, parameterization, coverage\n\n### [async-patterns.md](resources/async-patterns.md)\nasyncio, aiohttp, async context managers\n\n### [packaging.md](resources/packaging.md)\nBuilding packages, publishing to PyPI, versioning -->\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **cpp-dev-guidelines** - C++ development patterns\n- **error-tracking** - Sentry integration for Python\n- **skill-developer** - Creating and managing skills\n\n---\n\n**Skill Status**: COMPLETE ✅\n**Line Count**: < 450 ✅\n**Progressive Disclosure**: Resource files for details ✅\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:24:40.876Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing strict type safety and modern Python 3.12+ patterns.","zh":"适合需要严格类型安全和现代Python 3.12+模式的Python开发代理。","ja":"Python 3.12+の厳格な型セーフティとモダンなパターンを必要とするPython開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"엄격한 타입 안전성과 최신 Python 3.12+ 패턴이 필요한 Python 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de Python que necesitan una seguridad de tipo estricta y patrones de Python 3.12+ modernos.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement Python nécessitant une sécurité de type stricte et des modèles Python 3.12+ modernes.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine strenge Typsicherheit und moderne Python-3.12+-Muster benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de segurança de tipo estrita e padrões Python 3.12+ modernos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки Python, которым требуется строгая безопасность типов и современные модели Python 3.12+.","ar":" مثالي لعميل التطوير بايثون الذي يحتاج إلى سلامة نوع صارمة وأنماط بايثون 3.12+ الحديثة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce consistent coding standards using ruff formatting, strict typing with Pydantic v2 models, and async/await syntax, ensuring high-quality Python development with FastAPI.","zh":"赋予代理人使用ruff格式、Pydantic v2模型的严格类型和async/await语法来执行一致的编码标准，确保高质量的Python开发与FastAPI。","ja":"ruffフォーマット、Pydantic v2モデルの厳格な型指定、async/await構文を使用して一貫したコード規約を実施し、FastAPIを使用した高品質のPython開発を可能にします。","ko":"ruff 형식, Pydantic v2 모델의 엄격한 타이핑 및 async/await 구문을 사용하여 일관된 코드 표준을 적용하고, FastAPI를 사용한 고품질 Python 개발을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar normas de codificación coherentes utilizando el formato ruff, tipificación estricta con modelos Pydantic v2 y sintaxis async/await, lo que garantiza un desarrollo de Python de alta calidad con FastAPI.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des normes de codage cohérentes en utilisant le formatage ruff, la typification stricte avec des modèles Pydantic v2 et la syntaxe async/await, garantissant ainsi un développement Python de haute qualité avec FastAPI.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, konsistente Codierungsstandards mit ruff-Formatierung, strenger Typisierung mit Pydantic-v2-Modellen und async/await-Syntax durchzusetzen, was eine hochwertige Python-Entwicklung mit FastAPI sicherstellt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor padrões de codificação consistentes usando formatação ruff, digitação estrita com modelos Pydantic v2 e sintaxe async/await, garantindo desenvolvimento Python de alta qualidade com FastAPI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать постоянные стандарты кодирования с помощью форматирования ruff, строгой типизации с моделями Pydantic v2 и синтаксисом async/await, гарантируя качественное развитие Python с FastAPI.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على فرض معايير الترميز المتسقة باستخدام تنسيق ruff والتهجئة الصارمة مع نماذج Pydantic v2 وتنسيق async/await، مما يضمن تطوير بايثون عالي الجودة مع FastAPI."},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing consistent Python coding standards","Generating type-safe Pydantic models","Setting up modern Python 3.12+ projects with async/await"],"zh":["执行一致的Python编码标准","生成类型安全的Pydantic模型","使用async/await设置现代Python 3.12+项目"],"ja":["一貫したPythonコード規約を実施する","型セーフティのあるPydanticモデルを生成する","async/awaitを使用してモダンなPython 3.12+プロジェクトを設定する"],"ko":["일관된 Python 코딩 표준을 적용하는","타입 세이프티가 보장되는 Pydantic 모델을 생성하는","async/await를 사용하여 최신 Python 3.12+ 프로젝트를 설정하는"],"es":["Aplicar normas de codificación de Python coherentes","Generar modelos Pydantic seguros para tipos","Configurar proyectos de Python 3.12+ modernos con async/await"],"fr":["Appliquer des normes de codage Python cohérentes","Générer des modèles Pydantic sécurisés pour les types","Configurer des projets Python 3.12+ modernes avec async/await"],"de":["Konsistente Python-Codierungsstandards durchsetzen","Typsichere Pydantic-Modelle generieren","Moderne Python-3.12+-Projekte mit async/await einrichten"],"pt":["Impor padrões de codificação Python consistentes","Gerar modelos Pydantic seguros em termos de tipo","Configurar projetos Python 3.12+ modernos com async/await"],"ru":["Обеспечение постоянных стандартов кодирования Python","Генерация моделей Pydantic, безопасных для типов","Настройка современных проектов Python 3.12+ с async/await"],"ar":["فرض معايير الترميز المتسقة لبايثون","توليد نماذج Pydantic آمنة من النوع","تكوين مشاريع Python 3.12+ الحديثة مع async/await"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3.12+","Limited to FastAPI framework"],"zh":["需要Python 3.12+","仅限FastAPI框架"],"ja":["Python 3.12+が必要","FastAPIフレームワークのみ"],"ko":["Python 3.12+가 필요","FastAPI 프레임워크만 지원"],"es":["Requiere Python 3.12+","Limitado al marco de FastAPI"],"fr":["Nécessite Python 3.12+","Limité au framework FastAPI"],"de":["Benötigt Python 3.12+","Begrenzt auf das FastAPI-Framework"],"pt":["Exige Python 3.12+","Limitado ao framework FastAPI"],"ru":["Требуется Python 3.12+","Ограничен фреймворком FastAPI"],"ar":["يتطلب بايثون 3.12+","