-w...","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Grove Spec Writing para Plataformas de...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Grove Spec Writing для Многокористувальських Б...","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: Grove Spec Writing لمنصات المدونا...","en":"grove-spec-writing"},"description":{"zh":"Grove Spec Writing是一款多租户博客平台，使用AI智能代理技术提高开发效率","ja":"Grove Spec Writingは、マルチテナントブログプラットフォームで、AIエージェント技術を使用して開発効率を向上させます","ko":"Grove Spec Writing은 멀티테넌트 블로그 플랫폼으로, AI 에이전트 기술을 사용하여 개발 효율성을 향상시킵니다","es":"La plataforma de blog multi-tenant con grove-spec-writing es una herramienta de AI que permite a los desarrolladores crear y gestionar blogs de manera eficiente","fr":"La plateforme de blog multi-locataire avec grove-spec-writing est un outil d''IA qui permet aux développeurs de créer et de gérer des blogs de manière efficace","de":"Die Multi-Mandanten-Blog-Plattform mit grove-spec-writing ist ein KI-Tool, das es Entwicklern ermöglicht, Blogs effizient zu erstellen und zu verwalten","pt":"Grove Spec Writing é uma plataforma de blog multi-tenant para desenvolvedores, permitindo a criação de conteúdo de forma eficiente.","ru":"Grove Spec Writing - это многокористувальская платформа блогов для разработчиков, позволяющая создавать контент эффективно.","ar":"Grove Spec Writing هي منصة مدونات متعددة المستخدمين للمطورين، مما يسمح بإنشاء المحتوى بفعالية.","en":"Multi-tenant blog platform"},"definition":{"en":"Multi-tenant blog platform"},"features":{"zh":["多租户支持","AI智能代理技术","高性能博客平台","灵活的自定义选项","安全可靠的数据存储"],"ja":["マルチテナント対応","AIエージェント技術","高性能ブログプラットフォーム","柔軟なカスタマイズオプション","安全で信頼できるデータストレージ"],"ko":["멀티테넌트 지원","AI 에이전트 기술","고성능 블로그 플랫폼","유연한 커스터마이징 옵션","안전하고 신뢰할 수 있는 데이터 저장소"],"es":["Plataforma de blog multi-tenant","Escritura de especificaciones con grove-spec-writing","Gestión de contenido para múltiples usuarios","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo","Seguridad y escalabilidad"],"fr":["Plateforme de blog multi-locataire","Rédaction de spécifications avec grove-spec-writing","Gestion de contenu pour plusieurs utilisateurs","Intégration avec des outils de développement","Sécurité et évolutivité"],"de":["Multi-Mandanten-Blog-Plattform","Spezifikationsschreibung mit grove-spec-writing","Inhaltsverwaltung für mehrere Benutzer","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Sicherheit und Skalierbarkeit"],"pt":["Plataforma de blog multi-tenant","Criação de conteúdo eficiente","Integração com React e Node.js","Suporte a CLI","Escalabilidade e flexibilidade"],"ru":["Многокористувальская платформа блогов","Эффективное создание контента","Интеграция с React и Node.js","Поддержка CLI","Масштабируемость и гибкость"],"ar":["منصة مدونات متعددة المستخدمين","إنشاء المحتوى بفعالية","التكامل مع React و Node.js","دعم CLI","المرونة والتنوع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用Grove Spec Writing","什么是AI智能代理","Grove Spec Writing替代品","Grove Spec Writing vs 其他博客平台","Grove Spec Writing安装","Grove Spec Writing设置指南"],"ja":["Grove Spec Writingの使い方","AIエージェントとは","Grove Spec Writingの代替","Grove Spec Writing vs その他のブログプラットフォーム","Grove Spec Writingのインストール","Grove Spec Writingの設定ガイド"],"ko":["Grove Spec Writing 사용법","AI 에이전트란","Grove Spec Writing 대체","Grove Spec Writing vs 다른 블로그 플랫폼","Grove Spec Writing 설치","Grove Spec Writing 설정 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de AI para desarrollo","plataforma de blog multi-tenant","grove-spec-writing","cómo usar grove-spec-writing","alternativas a grove-spec-writing","instalación de grove-spec-writing","guía de configuración de grove-spec-writing"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour le développement","plateforme de blog multi-locataire","grove-spec-writing","comment utiliser grove-spec-writing","alternatives à grove-spec-writing","installation de grove-spec-writing","guide de configuration de grove-spec-writing"],"de":["KI-Tools für die Entwicklung","Multi-Mandanten-Blog-Plattform","grove-spec-writing","wie man grove-spec-writing verwendet","Alternativen zu grove-spec-writing","Installation von grove-spec-writing","Konfigurationshandbuch für grove-spec-writing"],"pt":["como usar Grove Spec Writing","o que é Grove Spec Writing","Grove Spec Writing vs WordPress","Grove Spec Writing alternativa","instalar Grove Spec Writing","guia de configuração do Grove Spec Writing"],"ru":["как использовать Grove Spec Writing","что такое Grove Spec Writing","Grove Spec Writing vs WordPress","Grove Spec Writing альтернатива","установить Grove Spec Writing","руководство по настройке Grove Spec Writing"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Grove Spec Writing","ما هي Grove Spec Writing","Grove Spec Writing مقابل WordPress","بديل Grove Spec Writing","تثبيت Grove Spec Writing","دليل إعداد Grove Spec Writing"]}},"owner":"AutumnsGrove","repo":"GroveEngine","repoPath":"AutumnsGrove/GroveEngine","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.937Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"grove-spec-writing","description":"Write and validate Grove technical specifications with consistent formatting, ASCII art headers, diagrams, and the Grove voice. Use when creating new specs, reviewing existing specs for completeness, or standardizing spec formatting.","bodyPreview":"# Grove Spec Writing\n\nA comprehensive guide for writing technical specifications in the Grove ecosystem. Use this skill to create new specs that feel like storybook entries, or to validate and standardize existing specs.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Creating a new technical specification\n- Reviewing an existing spec for completeness\n- Adding ASCII art headers to specs missing them\n- Adding diagrams, mockups, or visual elements to text-heavy specs\n- Standardizing frontmatter across spec files\n- Valida","body":"# Grove Spec Writing\n\nA comprehensive guide for writing technical specifications in the Grove ecosystem. Use this skill to create new specs that feel like storybook entries, or to validate and standardize existing specs.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Creating a new technical specification\n- Reviewing an existing spec for completeness\n- Adding ASCII art headers to specs missing them\n- Adding diagrams, mockups, or visual elements to text-heavy specs\n- Standardizing frontmatter across spec files\n- Validating a spec against Grove standards before finalizing\n\n---\n\n## The Spec as Storybook Entry\n\nGrove specs aren''t just technical documents. They''re **storybook entries** in a larger narrative. Each spec should feel like opening a page in a beautifully illustrated field guide to the forest.\n\n**The formula:**\n1. **Cover page** (frontmatter + ASCII art + tagline)\n2. **Introduction** (what is this, in nature and in Grove)\n3. **The journey** (architecture, flows, implementation)\n4. **The details** (API, schema, security)\n5. **The path forward** (implementation checklist)\n\n---\n\n## Required Structure\n\n### 1. Frontmatter (REQUIRED)\n\nEvery spec MUST have this exact frontmatter format:\n\n```yaml\n---\naliases: []\ndate created: [Day], [Month] [Ordinal] [Year]\ndate modified: [Day], [Month] [Ordinal] [Year]\ntags:\n  - primary-domain\n  - tech-stack\n  - category\ntype: tech-spec\n---\n```\n\n**Date format examples:**\n- `Monday, December 29th 2025`\n- `Saturday, January 4th 2026`\n\n**Type options:**\n- `tech-spec` — Technical specification (most common)\n- `implementation-plan` — Step-by-step implementation guide\n- `index` — Index/navigation document\n\n### 2. ASCII Art Header (REQUIRED)\n\nImmediately after frontmatter, include a code block with ASCII art that visually represents the concept:\n\n```\n# [Name] — [Short Description]\n\n```\n         ASCII ART HERE\n         representing the concept\n         in a visual way\n```\n\n> *Poetic tagline in italics*\n```\n\n**Good ASCII art:**\n- Relates to the nature metaphor (forest, garden, etc.)\n- Represents the concept visually (layers for backup, rings for analytics)\n- Uses box-drawing characters: `─│┌┐└┘├┤┬┴┼╭╮╰╯`\n- Uses nature emoji sparingly: `🌲🌿🍂✨🌸`\n- Includes a poetic tagline or motto\n\n**Examples from excellent specs:**\n\n**Wisp (will-o''-the-wisp light):**\n```\n         🌲  🌲  🌲\n          \\   |   /\n           \\  |  /\n             ✨\n            ╱ ╲\n           ╱   ╲\n          ╱  ·  ╲\n         ╱   ·   ╲\n        ╱    ·    ╲\n       ·     ·     ·\n         gentle\n         guiding\n          light\n```\n\n**Patina (layered backups):**\n```\n                     ╭───────────────────╮\n                    ╭┤  ┌─────────────┐  ├╮\n                   ╭┤│  │  2026-01-05 │  │├╮\n                   │││  │  ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ │  │││\n                   │││  │  ▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒ │  │││\n                   │││  │  ░░░░░░░░░░ │  │││\n                   │││  │  ·········· │  │││\n                   ╰┴┴──└─────────────┘──┴┴╯\n                  ╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n               ──────────────────────────────\n              ~~~~~~~~ oxidation layer ~~~~~~~~\n              Age as armor. Time as protection.\n```\n\n**Heartwood (tree rings):**\n```\n                      ╭──────────╮\n                   ╭──│ ╭──────╮ │──╮\n                 ╭─│  │ │ ╭──╮ │ │  │─╮\n                │  │  │ │ │♥ │ │ │  │  │\n                 ╰─│  │ │ ╰──╯ │ │  │─╯\n                   ╰──│ ╰──────╯ │──╯\n                      ╰──────────╯\n\n       every ring: a year, a story, a layer of growth\n\n               The center that holds it all.\n```\n\n### 3. Introduction Section\n\nAfter the ASCII art header:\n\n```markdown\n> *Poetic tagline repeated*\n\n[2-3 sentence description of what this is in the Grove ecosystem]\n\n**Public Name:** [Name]\n**Internal Name:** Grove[Name]\n**Domain:** `name.grove.place`\n**Repository:** [Link if applicable]\n**Last Updated:** [Month Year]\n\n[1-2 paragraphs explaining the nature metaphor and how it applies]\n\n---\n```\n\n### 4. Body Sections\n\nOrganize content with clear headers. Include:\n\n- **Overview/Goals** — What this system does\n- **Architecture** — How it''s built (with diagrams!)\n- **Tech Stack** — Dependencies, frameworks\n- **API/Schema** — Technical details\n- **Security** — Important considerations\n- **Implementation Checklist** — Clear action items\n\n---\n\n## Required Visual Elements\n\n### Flow Diagrams\n\nEvery spec describing a process MUST include at least one ASCII flow diagram:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                         Client Sites                                │\n│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐               │\n│  │   Site A     │  │   Site B     │  │   Site C     │               │\n│  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘               │\n└─────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────┼───────────────────────┘\n          │                 │                 │\n          │    1. Request   │                 │\n          ▼                 ▼                 ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        Central Service                              │\n│                                                                     │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────────┐           │\n│  │      Handler A          │  │      Handler B          │           │\n│  └─────────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────────┘           │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Box drawing reference:**\n- Corners: `┌ ┐ └ ┘` (square) or `╭ ╮ ╰ ╯` (rounded)\n- Lines: `─ │ ═ ║`\n- Joins: `├ ┤ ┬ ┴ ┼`\n- Arrows: `→ ← ↑ ↓ ▶ ◀ ▲ ▼`\n\n### UI Mockups\n\nSpecs describing user interfaces MUST include ASCII mockups:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ✧ Panel Title                                          [×]      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                 │\n│  ┌─ Label ────────────────────────────────────────────────┐     │\n│  │ Content here with proper spacing                       │     │\n│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘     │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\n│  │ Input field...                                     [↵]  │    │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────    │\n│  [ Action A ]                              [ Action B ✦ ]       │\n│                                                                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### State Diagrams\n\nFor features with multiple states:\n\n```\n   Idle:                    Analyzing:               Success:\n   .  *  .    .  *         . * . analyzing . *           *\n  .    _    .      .         \\  |  /             .    *  /|\\   .\n     /   \\    *  .         -- (o.o) --  thinking    *   / | \\    *\n    / ~ ~ \\  .    .          /  |  \\                   /__|__\\\n   /       \\______        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ~~~~/       \\~~~~\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       words flowing...        all clear\n```\n\n### Comparison Tables\n\nUse tables to compare options, states, or configurations:\n\n```markdown\n| Feature | Seedling | Sapling | Oak | Evergreen |\n|---------|----------|---------|-----|-----------|\n| Posts   | 50       | 250     | ∞   | ∞         |\n| Storage | 1 GB     | 5 GB    | 20 GB | 100 GB  |\n| Themes  | 3        | 10      | All | All + custom |\n```\n\n### Timeline/Retention Diagrams\n\nFor anything involving time:\n\n```\n  TODAY                                              12 WEEKS AGO\n    │                                                      │\n    ▼                                                      ▼\n   ┌─┬─┬─┬─┬─┬─┬─┐                                        ┌─┐\n   │█│█│█│█│█│█│█│ ◀── Daily backups (7 days)             │░│\n   └─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┘                                        └─┘\n   S M T W T F S\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing any spec, verify:\n\n### Structure\n- [ ] Frontmatter present with all required fields\n- [ ] `aliases: []` included (even if empty)\n- [ ] Date format correct (Day, Month Ordinal Year)\n- [ ] `type: tech-spec` or appropriate type\n- [ ] ASCII art header present after frontmatter\n- [ ] Poetic tagline in italics\n- [ ] Public/Internal names listed\n- [ ] Domain specified (if applicable)\n\n### Visual Content\n- [ ] At least one ASCII flow diagram (if process-based)\n- [ ] UI mockups included (if describing interface)\n- [ ] Tables for comparisons where appropriate\n- [ ] Code blocks for technical details\n- [ ] No walls of text without visual breaks\n\n### Voice (refer to grove-documentation skill)\n- [ ] No em-dashes (use periods or commas)\n- [ ] No \"not X, but Y\" patterns\n- [ ] No AI-coded words (robust, seamless, leverage, etc.)\n- [ ] Short paragraphs\n- [ ] Poetic closers earned, not forced\n\n### Completeness\n- [ ] Overview/Goals section\n- [ ] Architecture diagram\n- [ ] Technical details (API, schema)\n- [ ] Security considerations\n- [ ] Implementation checklist\n\n---\n\n## Creating ASCII Art\n\n### The Process\n\n1. **Identify the core metaphor** — What natural thing does this represent?\n2. **Sketch the concept** — What visual would convey this at a glance?\n3. **Choose your characters** — Box drawing, emoji, or creative ASCII\n4. **Build in layers** — Start with outline, add detail, add flourishes\n5. **Add the tagline** — Poetic one-liner that captures the essence\n\n### Character Palette\n\n**Box Drawing (safe, consistent):**\n```\n┌─────┬─────┐    ╭─────╮\n│     │     │    │     │\n├─────┼─────┤    ╰─────╯\n│     │     │\n└─────┴─────┘\n```\n\n**Lines and Arrows:**\n```\n→ ← ↑ ↓ ↔ ↕\n▶ ◀ ▲ ▼\n⟿ ⟸ ⟹\n```\n\n**Nature Emoji (use sparingly):**\n```\n🌲 🌳 🌿 🍂 🍃 🌸 🌺 🌻 🌷 🌱 🍄\n☀️ 🌤️ ⭐ ✨ 💧 🔥\n🦋 🐛 🐌\n```\n\n**Decorative:**\n```\n· ∙ • ° ˚ ∘\n~ ≈ ∿\n═ ║ ╔ ╗ ╚ ╝\n░ ▒ ▓ █\n```\n\n### Tips\n\n- Keep ASCII art under 20 lines tall\n- Center the art within its code block\n- Include breathing room (empty lines above/below)\n- Test in a monospace font\n- Consider mobile rendering (simpler is better)\n\n---\n\n## Example: Complete Spec Header\n\n```markdown\n---\naliases: []\ndate created: Monday, January 6th 2026\ndate modified: Monday, January 13th 2026\ntags:\n  - support\n  - user-communication\n  - cloudflare-workers\ntype: tech-spec\n---\n\n# Porch — Support System\n\n```\n                              🏠\n                           ___│___\n                          │       │\n                    ~~~~~~│ PORCH │~~~~~~\n                         ╱│_______│╲\n                        ╱           ╲\n                       ╱  ┌───┐      ╲\n                      ╱   │ ☕ │       ╲\n                     ╱    └───┘ 👤     ╲\n                    ════════════════════════\n                           steps\n\n              Have a seat. We''ll figure it out.\n```\n\n> *Have a seat on the porch. We''ll figure it out together.*\n\nGrove''s front porch: a warm, accessible space where users sit down and have a conversation. Not a corporate help desk with ticket numbers. A porch where you chat with the grove keeper about what''s going on.\n\n**Public Name:** Porch\n**Internal Name:** GrovePorch\n**Domain:** `porch.grove.place`\n**Status:** Planned (Launch Priority)\n\nA porch is where you sit and talk. You come up the steps, have a seat, and the grove keeper comes out to chat. It''s not a ticket counter. It''s two people on a porch, figuring things out together.\n\n---\n```\n\n---\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n### Before Writing a Spec\n\n1. **walking-through-the-grove** — If naming a new feature, complete the naming journey first\n2. **grove-ui-design** — If the spec involves UI, understand design patterns\n\n### While Writing\n\n3. **grove-documentation** — Apply Grove voice throughout, avoid AI patterns\n\n### After Writing\n\n4. **grove-spec-writing** (this skill) — Run validation checklist\n5. Review with fresh eyes: Does it feel like a storybook entry?\n\n### When to Use museum-documentation Instead\n\nThis skill (grove-spec-writing) is for **internal technical specifications**: architecture decisions, system design, implementation plans. Documentation for developers.\n\nUse **museum-documentation** when writing for **Wanderers who want to understand**:\n\n| Use grove-spec-writing | Use museum-documentation |\n|-----------------------|-------------------------|\n| Technical specifications | \"How it works\" for curious visitors |\n| Architecture decisions | Codebase guided tours |\n| Implementation plans | Knowledge base exhibits |\n| Internal system docs | Narrative technical explanations |\n\nIf the reader is a **developer implementing something**, use this skill.\nIf the reader is a **Wanderer exploring the forest**, use museum-documentation.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Element | Required | Location |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| Frontmatter | Yes | Top of file |\n| ASCII art header | Yes | After frontmatter |\n| Poetic tagline | Yes | After ASCII art |\n| Public/Internal names | Yes | Introduction |\n| Architecture diagram | If applicable | Body |\n| UI mockups | If has UI | Body |\n| Implementation checklist | Yes | End of spec |\n\n---\n\n*A good spec is one you''d want to read at 2 AM. Make it beautiful.*\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:35:22.268Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing standardized specification generation in the Grove ecosystem.","zh":"非常适合需要在 Grove 生态系统中生成标准化规范的技术写作代理","ja":"Grove エコシステムで標準化された仕様を生成する必要があるテクニカルライティングエージェントに最適","ko":"Grove 생태계에서 표준화된 사양을 생성해야 하는 기술 작성 에이전트에게 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Escritura Técnica que necesitan generación de especificaciones estandarizadas en el ecosistema Grove.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Écriture Technique ayant besoin de génération de spécifications standardisées dans l''écosystème Grove.","de":"Perfekt für technische Schreibagenten, die standardisierte Spezifikationserstellung im Grove-Ökosystem benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Escrita Técnica que necessitam de geração de especificações padronizadas no ecossistema Grove.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов технической документации, которым требуется генерация стандартизированных спецификаций в экосистеме Grove.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الكتابة الفنية الذين يحتاجون إلى توليد مواصفات معيارية في نظام Grove."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and validate technical specifications with standardized frontmatter, ASCII art headers, and visual elements like diagrams and mockups, ensuring consistency across spec files.","zh":"赋予代理创建和验证技术规范的能力，具有标准化的前置内容、ASCII 艺术标题和视觉元素，如图表和模拟，确保规格文件的一致性","ja":"エージェントが標準化されたフロントマター、ASCII アートヘッダー、図やモックアップなどの視覚要素を持つ技術仕様を作成して検証する能力を提供し、仕様ファイルの整合性を確保","ko":"에이전트가 표준화된 프론티어, ASCII 아트 헤더 및 다이어그램, 모의 업などの 시각적 요소를 갖춘 기술 사양을 생성 및 검증할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 사양 파일의 일관성을 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y validar especificaciones técnicas con frontmatter estandarizado, encabezados de arte ASCII y elementos visuales como diagramas y maquetas, garantizando la consistencia en los archivos de especificaciones.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de valider des spécifications techniques avec un frontmatter standardisé, des en-têtes d''art ASCII et des éléments visuels tels que des diagrammes et des maquettes, garantissant la cohérence entre les fichiers de spécifications.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, technische Spezifikationen mit standardisiertem Frontmatter, ASCII-Kunst-Headern und visuellen Elementen wie Diagrammen und Mockups zu erstellen und zu validieren, um Konsistenz über Spezifikationsdateien hinweg sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e validar especificações técnicas com frontmatter padronizado, cabeçalhos de arte ASCII e elementos visuais como diagramas e protótipos, garantindo consistência em todos os arquivos de especificações.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать и проверять технические спецификации с стандартизированным frontmatter, заголовками ASCII-искусства и визуальными элементами, такими как диаграммы и макеты, обеспечивая последовательность во всех файлах спецификаций.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء وتحقق المواصفات الفنية مع.frontmatter معياري ، عناوين فنية ASCII ، وعناصر بصرية مثل الرسومات والنماذج ، مما يضمن الاتساق في جميع ملفات المواصفات."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating new technical specifications with storybook-like entries","Validating and standardizing existing specs for completeness and consistency","Adding visual elements to text-heavy specs for enhanced readability"],"zh":["生成具有 storybook-like 条目的新技术规范","验证和标准化现有的规格以确保完整性和一致性","向文本密集的规格添加视觉元素以提高可读性"],"ja":["storybook-like エントリを持つ新しい技術仕様を生成","既存の仕様を検証して標準化し、完備性と整合性を確保","テキスト密度の高い仕様に視覚要素を追加して可読性を高める"],"ko":["storybook-like 항목을 갖춘 새로운 기술 사양 생성","기존 사양의 유효성과 일致성을 확인하고 표준화","텍스트가 많은 사양에 시각적 요소를 추가하여 가독성을 높임"],"es":["Generación de nuevas especificaciones técnicas con entradas tipo storybook","Validación y estandarización de especificaciones existentes para completitud y consistencia","Adición de elementos visuales a especificaciones textuales para mejorar la legibilidad"],"fr":["Génération de nouvelles spécifications techniques avec des entrées de type storybook","Validation et standardisation de spécifications existantes pour l''exhaustivité et la cohérence","Ajout d''éléments visuels à des spécifications textuelles pour améliorer la lisibilité"],"de":["Erstellung neuer technischer Spezifikationen mit storybook-ähnlichen Einträgen","Validierung und Standardisierung bestehender Spezifikationen für Vollständigkeit und Konsistenz","Hinzufügen von visuellen Elementen zu textlastigen Spezifikationen für verbesserte Lesbarkeit"],"pt":["Geração de novas especificações técnicas com entradas semelhantes a storybook","Validação e padronização de especificações existentes para completeza e consistência","Adição de elementos visuais a especificações textuais para melhorar a legibilidade"],"ru":["Генерация новых технических спецификаций со страницами, подобными storybook","Проверка и стандартизация существующих спецификаций на полноту и последовательность","Добавление визуальных элементов к текстовым спецификациям для улучшения читаемости"],"ar":["توليد مواصفات فنية جديدة مع مدخلات شبيهة bởi storybook","التحقق والتوحيد للمواصفات الحالية للكامل والاتساق","إضافة عناصر بصرية إلى المواصفات النصية لتحسين القراءة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of the Grove ecosystem","Limited to technical specification writing","Dependent on the quality of input data for validation and standardization"],"zh":["需要了解 Grove 生态系统","仅限于技术规范的编写","依赖于输入数据的质量以进行验证和标准化"],"ja":["Grove エコシステムの知識が必要","技術仕様の作成のみに限定","入力データの品質に依存して検証と標準化を行う"],"ko":["Grove 생태계에 대한 지식이 필요","기술 사양 작성에만 제한","입력 데이터의 품질에 따라 유효성과 표준화를 수행"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del ecosistema Grove","Limitado a la escritura de especificaciones técnicas","Dependiente de la calidad de los datos de entrada para la validación y estandarización"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance de l''écosystème Grove","Limité à la rédaction de spécifications techniques","Dépend de la qualité des données d''entrée pour la validation et la standardisation"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse des Grove-Ökosystems","Begrenzt auf die Erstellung technischer Spezifikationen","Abhängig von der Qualität der Eingabedaten für Validierung und Standardisierung"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento do ecossistema Grove","Limitado à escrita de especificações técnicas","Dependente da qualidade dos dados de entrada para validação e padronização"],"ru":["Требует знания экосистемы Grove","Ограничен написанием технических спецификаций","Зависит от качества входных данных для проверки и стандартизации"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بنية Grove","محدود بالكتابة الفنية للمواصفات","يعتمد على جودة البيانات المُدخلة للتحقق والتوحيد"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"5bbb13eb32ebf94593fce9ee588edb50e66ba39347041a7a06947e3d94d48ad4","qualityScore":52}');
