r":"أدوات البحث الاجتماعي مع LLMs - تحليل التجارب","en":"analyze-experiment"},"description":{"zh":"analyze-experiment工具提供了使用LLMs进行社会研究的功能，支持数据分析和实验设计","ja":"analyze-experimentツールはLLMsを使用した社会研究をサポートし、データ分析と実験設計が可能","ko":"analyze-experiment 도구는 LLMs를 사용한 사회 연구를 지원하며 데이터 분석과 실험 설계가 가능","es":"La habilidad analyze-experiment ofrece herramientas para la investigación social con LLMs. Ayuda a los desarrolladores a mejorar sus proyectos con Agentes de IA","fr":"La compétence analyze-experiment propose des outils pour la recherche sociale avec LLMs. Aide les développeurs à améliorer leurs projets avec Agents IA","de":"Die Fähigkeit analyze-experiment bietet Tools für die soziale Forschung mit LLMs. Hilft Entwicklern, ihre Projekte mit KI-Agenten zu verbessern","pt":"As ferramentas de análise de experimentos com LLMs permitem que os desenvolvedores conduzam pesquisas sociais de forma eficaz","ru":"ИИ Агенты для анализа экспериментов с LLMs позволяют разработчикам проводить социальные исследования эффективно","ar":"أدوات تحليل التجارب مع LLMs تمكن المطورين من إجراء بحوث اجتماعية بفعالية","en":"Tools for conducting social research with LLMs"},"definition":{"en":"Tools for conducting social research with LLMs"},"features":{"zh":["支持LLMs进行数据分析","提供实验设计和实施功能","支持多种数据格式","集成React和Python开发环境","提供CLI接口","支持Node.js集成"],"ja":["LLMsを使用したデータ分析のサポート","実験設計と実施の機能","多種のデータ形式のサポート","ReactとPython開発環境の統合","CLIインターフェースの提供","Node.jsとの統合のサポート"],"ko":["LLMs를 사용한 데이터 분석 지원","실험 설계와实施 기능","다양한 데이터 형식 지원","React와 Python 개발 환경 통합","CLI 인터페이스 제공","Node.js와의 통합 지원"],"es":["Herramientas de investigación social con LLMs","Integración con Agentes de IA","Análisis de datos sociales","Desarrollo de proyectos con React y Node.js","Uso de CLI para Agentes de IA","Compatibilidad con Python"],"fr":["Outils de recherche sociale avec LLMs","Intégration avec Agents IA","Analyse de données sociales","Développement de projets avec React et Node.js","Utilisation de CLI pour Agents IA","Compatibilité avec Python"],"de":["Soziale Forschungstools mit LLMs","Integration mit KI-Agenten","Analyse sozialer Daten","Entwicklung von Projekten mit React und Node.js","Verwendung von CLI für KI-Agenten","Kompatibilität mit Python"],"pt":["Análise de dados sociais com LLMs","Ferramentas de pesquisa social avançadas","Integração com bibliotecas de desenvolvimento","Suporte a múltiplos formatos de dados","Análise de experimentos personalizável"],"ru":["Анализ социальных данных с ИИ Агентами","Продвинутые инструменты социальных исследований","Интеграция с библиотеками разработки","Поддержка нескольких форматов данных","Настройка анализа экспериментов"],"ar":["تحليل البيانات الاجتماعية مع LLMs","أدوات بحث اجتماعي متقدمة","التكامل مع مكتبات التطوير","دعم صيغ بيانات متعددة","تحليل تجارب قابل للتعديل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用analyze-experiment工具","什么是LLMs","analyze-experiment工具替代品","analyze-experiment工具与竞争对手比较","analyze-experiment工具安装","analyze-experiment工具设置指南","使用React和Python进行社会研究","LLMs在社会研究中的应用"],"ja":["analyze-experimentツールの使い方","LLMsとは","analyze-experimentツールの代替","analyze-experimentツールと競合ツールの比較","analyze-experimentツールのインストール","analyze-experimentツールの設定ガイド","ReactとPythonを使用した社会研究","LLMsを使用した社会研究の応用"],"ko":["analyze-experiment 도구 사용법","LLMs是什么","analyze-experiment 도구 대체","analyze-experiment 도구와 경쟁 도구 비교","analyze-experiment 도구 설치","analyze-experiment 도구 설정 가이드","React와 Python을 사용한 사회 연구","LLMs를 사용한 사회 연구의 응용"],"es":["cómo utilizar Agentes de IA","qué es analyze-experiment","herramientas de investigación social","Agentes de IA alternativos","analyze-experiment vs otros","instalación de Agentes de IA","guía de configuración de Agentes de IA","desarrollo de proyectos con Agentes de IA"],"fr":["comment utiliser les Agents IA","qu''est-ce que analyze-experiment","outils de recherche sociale","Agents IA alternatifs","analyze-experiment vs autres","installation d''Agents IA","guide de configuration d''Agents IA","développement de projets avec Agents IA"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten verwendet","was ist analyze-experiment","soziale Forschungstools","KI-Agenten-Alternativen","analyze-experiment vs andere","Installation von KI-Agenten","Konfigurationsanleitung für KI-Agenten","Entwicklung von Projekten mit KI-Agenten"],"pt":["como usar LLMs","o que é análise de experimentos","ferramentas de pesquisa social","análise de dados sociais","LLMs para desenvolvedores","análise de experimentos com Python","alternativas para LLMs","guia de instalação de LLMs"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое анализ экспериментов","инструменты социальных исследований","анализ социальных данных","ИИ Агенты для разработчиков","анализ экспериментов с Python","альтернативы для ИИ Агентов","руководство по установке ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام LLMs","ما هو تحليل التجارب","أدوات البحث الاجتماعي","تحليل البيانات الاجتماعية","LLMs للمطورين","تحليل التجارب مع Python","بديل ل LLMs","دليل تثبيت LLMs"]}},"owner":"niznik-dev","repo":"cruijff_kit","repoPath":"niznik-dev/cruijff_kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:11.096Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"analyze-experiment","description":"Generate visualizations from completed experiment evaluations using inspect-viz. Use after run-experiment to create interactive HTML plots from inspect-ai evaluation logs.","bodyPreview":"# Analyze Experiment\n\nYou help users visualize and analyze results from completed experiments by generating interactive HTML and PNG plots using inspect-viz pre-built views.\n\n## Your Task\n\nGenerate visualizations from evaluation results:\n\n1. Read experiment_summary.yaml to understand experimental design\n2. Load evaluation logs from run directories\n3. Infer appropriate visualization types based on experimental variables\n4. Generate interactive HTML plots using inspect-viz\n5. Log the process in lo","body":"# Analyze Experiment\n\nYou help users visualize and analyze results from completed experiments by generating interactive HTML and PNG plots using inspect-viz pre-built views.\n\n## Your Task\n\nGenerate visualizations from evaluation results:\n\n1. Read experiment_summary.yaml to understand experimental design\n2. Load evaluation logs from run directories\n3. Infer appropriate visualization types based on experimental variables\n4. Generate interactive HTML plots using inspect-viz\n5. Log the process in logs/analyze-experiment.log\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- experiment_summary.yaml exists (from design-experiment)\n- Evaluations complete (from run-experiment)\n- inspect-viz installed (`pip install inspect-viz`)\n- Conda environment activated (from claude.local.md)\n- **Optional:** playwright for PNG export (`pip install playwright && playwright install chromium`)\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Locate Experiment → `parsing.md`\n\nFind experiment directory and parse experiment_summary.yaml for:\n- Experimental variables (model, task, factors)\n- Run structure and naming conventions\n- Evaluation matrix\n\n**See `parsing.md` for:**\n- How to find the experiment directory\n- YAML parsing logic\n- Extracting variable types for inference\n\n### 2. Load Evaluation Logs → `data_loading.md`\n\nUse helper functions from `tools/inspect/viz_helpers.py`:\n- `deduplicate_eval_files()` - Remove duplicate evals (keeps most recent per model+epoch)\n- `evals_df_prep()` - Prepare eval-level dataframes\n- `parse_eval_metadata()` - Extract epoch/finetuned/source_model from JSON metadata\n- `detect_metrics()` - Dynamically detect available score columns\n\n**See `data_loading.md` for:**\n- Automatic deduplication of re-run evaluations\n- Generic metadata extraction using vis_label and JSON metadata\n- How to construct subdirs list from experiment_summary.yaml\n- Preparing data for each view type\n\n### 3. Select Visualizations\n\nMap experimental variables to appropriate pre-built views:\n\n| Variable Type | View |\n|---------------|------|\n| Multiple models | `scores_by_model` |\n| Binary factor | `scores_by_factor` |\n| Multiple tasks/conditions | `scores_by_task` |\n| Model × task matrix | `scores_heatmap` |\n| Multiple metrics | `scores_radar_by_task` |\n\n### 4. Generate Plots → `generation.md`\n\nCreate visualizations using inspect-viz:\n1. Wrap dataframes with `Data.from_dataframe()`\n2. Call appropriate pre-built view functions\n3. Save HTML with `write_html()`\n4. Auto-export PNG with `write_png()` if playwright is available\n\n**See `generation.md` for:**\n- Dynamic metric detection\n- View function signatures and parameters\n- PNG export with playwright auto-detection\n- Output file naming conventions\n- Creating multiple plots per experiment\n\n### 5. Generate Analysis & Interpretation → `generation.md`\n\n**This step is required by default.** Write a `future_directions` string that interprets the results and suggests next steps. This section should:\n\n1. Interpret the key findings (what do the metrics mean for the research question?)\n2. Note any surprises or anomalies in the results\n3. Suggest concrete next experiments or analyses\n\nOnly omit this section if the user explicitly asks to skip it.\n\n### 6. Generate Report → `generation.md`\n\nCreate markdown report with metrics and comparisons:\n1. Extract metrics from evaluation dataframe\n2. Compute Wilson score confidence intervals\n3. Generate narrative summary and comparison tables\n4. Include `future_directions` from step 5\n5. Write report to `analysis/report.md`\n\nUses `tools/inspect/report_generator.py`:\n```python\nfrom tools.inspect.report_generator import generate_report\n\nreport = generate_report(\n    df=logs_df,\n    experiment_name=experiment_name,\n    output_path=Path(experiment_dir) / \"analysis\" / \"report.md\",\n    config=experiment_config,  # Optional, for research question metadata\n    future_directions=future_directions,  # From step 5\n)\n```\n\n### 6b. Compute Utilization Report → `generation.md`\n\nIf run logs exist (`logs/run-torchtune.log` and/or `logs/run-inspect.log`), generate a compute utilization section:\n\n1. Extract job IDs from logs (regex: `Result: Job ID (\\d+)`)\n2. Run `seff` for each job and parse with `tools/slurm/compute_metrics.py`\n3. Read `gpu_metrics.csv` files and summarize with `summarize_gpu_metrics()`\n4. Generate compute table with `format_compute_table()`\n5. Save raw metrics to `analysis/compute_metrics.json`\n6. Pass formatted table as `compute_section` to `generate_report()`\n\n**Skip silently** if no run logs exist (e.g., analyzing results without having run the experiment locally).\n\n### 7. Logging → `logging.md`\n\nDocument process in `{experiment_dir}/logs/analyze-experiment.log`\n\n**See `logging.md` for:**\n- JSONL format specification\n- Action types (LOCATE, PARSE, LOAD, INFER, GENERATE)\n- Example log entries\n\n---\n\n## Supported Pre-built Views\n\n| View | Use Case | Required Data |\n|------|----------|---------------|\n| `scores_by_task` | Multiple tasks/conditions | task_name column |\n| `scores_heatmap` | Model × task matrix | model + task columns |\n| `scores_radar_by_task` | Multiple metrics | Multiple score columns |\n| `scores_by_factor` | Binary factors | Boolean factor column |\n| `scores_by_model` | Cross-model comparison (single task only) | model column, single task |\n\n**Note:** `scores_by_model` requires a single-task experiment. For multi-task experiments, use `scores_by_task`, `scores_heatmap`, or `scores_radar_by_task` instead.\n\n## User Questions\n\n### Existing Analysis Outputs\n\nIf `analysis/` directory exists with files, **ask the user**:\n\n```\nFound existing analysis outputs in analysis/. What would you like to do?\n\n1. Keep existing files, add new outputs (Recommended)\n2. Clean analysis directory first\n```\n\nIf user chooses option 2, delete contents of `analysis/` before generating new outputs.\n\n### Visualization Selection\n\nWhen `vis_label` creates multiple task variants (conditions), **ask the user** which visualization to generate:\n\n```\nFound {N} conditions via vis_label: {list}\n\nWhich visualization would you like?\n\n1. scores_by_task - Compare conditions side-by-side (Recommended)\n2. scores_heatmap - Model × condition matrix\n3. Both\n```\n\n### Tracking Generated Files\n\n**Important:** Track which PNG files you generate during this run. Only pass those to `generate_report()` so the report embeds only the visualizations created in this session, not stale outputs from previous runs.\n\n```python\ngenerated_pngs = []\n\n# After each successful PNG export\ngenerated_pngs.append(png_path)\n\n# Pass to report generator\ngenerate_report(..., generated_pngs=generated_pngs)\n```\n\n**Smart defaults for everything else:**\n- Deduplication: Automatic (keep most recent per model+epoch)\n- Epochs: Use latest only (unless user explicitly asks for all)\n- Metrics: Plot all available (dynamically detected)\n- PNG: Auto-detect playwright; generate if available, skip with warning if not\n\n## Output Structure\n\nAfter running, the experiment directory will contain:\n\n```\n{experiment_dir}/\n├── analysis/\n│   ├── report.md               # Markdown report with metrics\n│   ├── scores_by_task.html\n│   ├── scores_by_task.png      (if playwright available)\n│   ├── scores_heatmap.html\n│   ├── scores_heatmap.png      (if playwright available)\n│   ├── roc_curves.png          (if risk_scorer used)\n│   ├── calibration_curves.png  (if risk_scorer used)\n│   ├── prediction_histogram.png (if risk_scorer used)\n│   └── ...\n├── logs/\n│   └── analyze-experiment.log\n└── experiment_summary.yaml\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n**If experiment_summary.yaml not found:**\n- Report error to user\n- Suggest running design-experiment skill first\n- Do not proceed\n\n**If no evaluation logs found:**\n- Report error to user\n- Suggest running run-experiment skill first\n- Do not proceed\n\n**If visualization generation fails:**\n- Log error details in analyze-experiment.log\n- Continue with remaining visualizations\n- Report which visualizations failed in summary\n\n**If inference cannot determine view type:**\n- Log warning\n- Ask user which view to generate\n- Or skip and note in summary\n\n## Validation Before Completion\n\nBefore reporting success, verify:\n- ✓ experiment_summary.yaml was found and parsed\n- ✓ Evaluation logs were loaded successfully\n- ✓ At least one visualization was generated\n- ✓ HTML files exist in analysis/ directory\n- ✓ report.md was generated in analysis/ directory\n- ✓ Log file created (logs/analyze-experiment.log)\n\n## Output Summary\n\nAfter completing analysis, provide a summary:\n\n```markdown\n## Analyze Experiment Complete\n\nExperiment: `{experiment_dir}`\n\n### Report Generated\n\n✓ Markdown report: `analysis/report.md`\n  - Executive summary with best performer\n  - Model comparison table with 95% CIs\n  - Calibration metrics (if available)\n\n### Visualizations Generated\n\n✓ {N} visualizations created in `analysis/`\n\n**Created:**\n- scores_by_task.html - Task comparison (match accuracy)\n- scores_heatmap.html - Model × task matrix\n- scores_by_model.html - Model comparison\n\n### Viewing Results\n\nOpen HTML files in a browser:\n```bash\nopen {experiment_dir}/analysis/scores_by_task.html\n```\n\nOr start a local server:\n```bash\ncd {experiment_dir}/analysis && python -m http.server 8080\n```\n\n### Log\n\nDetails recorded in `logs/analyze-experiment.log`\n\n### Report Path\n\n`{experiment_dir}/analysis/report.md`\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Always end your output summary with the **full absolute path** to `report.md` on its own line, so the user can command-click it in their terminal/IDE. Example:\n\n```\nFull report: /scratch/gpfs/user/ck-experiments/my_experiment/analysis/report.md\n```\n\n## Relationship to Other Skills\n\n- **After:** run-experiment, summarize-experiment\n- **Reads:** experiment_summary.yaml, .eval files\n- **Creates:** HTML visualizations, analysis log\n\n**Workflow position:**\n```\ndesign-experiment → scaffold-experiment → run-experiment → analyze-experiment\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **Metadata-driven** - uses `vis_label` metadata for task names, JSON metadata for epoch/finetuned/source_model\n- **Automatic deduplication** - when multiple evals exist for the same model+epoch, keeps only the most recent (logs skipped files)\n- **Dynamic metric detection** - plots all available score columns (no hardcoding)\n- **Must run after evaluations complete** - requires .eval files to exist\n- Visualizations are independent - one failing doesn''t stop others\n- Output directory (`analysis/`) is created if it doesn''t exist\n- HTML files are standalone (no external dependencies to view)\n- PNG files require playwright (skipped with warning if not installed)\n- Uses helper functions from `tools/inspect/viz_helpers.py`\n- Reference examples in `viz_examples/scripts/inspect_viz_examples.ipynb`\n\n## Module Organization\n\n| Module | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| parsing.md | Experiment location and YAML parsing |\n| data_loading.md | Helper functions for loading logs |\n| generation.md | Plot creation workflow |\n| logging.md | JSONL audit trail specification |\n\n## Implementation Reference\n\nWorking examples exist in `viz_examples/scripts/inspect_viz_examples.ipynb` demonstrating all supported pre-built views.\n\nHelper functions are implemented in `tools/inspect/viz_helpers.py`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:32:28.542Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced experiment visualization capabilities with YAML and HTML plots.","zh":"非常适合需要高级实验可视化能力的数据分析代理，支持YAML和HTML绘图。","ja":"データ分析エージェントが高度な実験可視化機能を必要とする場合に適しています。YAMLおよびHTMLプロットをサポートします。","ko":"데이터 분석 에이전트가 고급 실험 시각화 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다. YAML 및 HTML 플롯을 지원합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de visualización de experimentos con YAML y tramas HTML.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''Analyse de Données nécessitant des capacités de visualisation d''expériences avancées avec YAML et des trames HTML.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte Experimentvisualisierungsfunktionen mit YAML und HTML-Plots benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de visualização de experimentos com YAML e tramas HTML.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности визуализации экспериментов с YAML и HTML-плотами.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء تحليل البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتصور التجارب مع YAML ورسومات HTML."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate interactive HTML plots using inspect-viz, infer visualization types from experimental variables, and log processes in log files, all while leveraging YAML configuration files like experiment_summary.yaml.","zh":"赋予代理生成交互式HTML绘图的能力，使用inspect-viz，根据实验变量推断可视化类型，并在日志文件中记录进程，同时利用YAML配置文件，如experiment_summary.yaml。","ja":"エージェントに、inspect-vizを使用してインタラクティブなHTMLプロットを生成し、実験変数から視覚化タイプを推測し、ログファイルにプロセスを記録する機能を提供します。同時に、experiment_summary.yamlのようなYAML設定ファイルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 inspect-viz를 사용하여 상호작용형 HTML 플롯을 생성하고 실험 변수에서 시각화 유형을 추론하며 로그 파일에 프로세스를 기록할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다.同时, experiment_summary.yaml 같은 YAML 구성 파일을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar tramas HTML interactivas usando inspect-viz, inferir tipos de visualización a partir de variables experimentales y registrar procesos en archivos de registro, todo mientras aprovecha archivos de configuración YAML como experiment_summary.yaml.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des trames HTML interactives à l''aide d''inspect-viz, d''inférer les types de visualisation à partir de variables expérimentales et de consigner les processus dans des fichiers de journal, le tout en exploitant des fichiers de configuration YAML comme experiment_summary.yaml.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, interaktive HTML-Plots mit inspect-viz zu generieren, Visualisierungstypen aus experimentellen Variablen abzuleiten und Prozesse in Log-Dateien zu protokollieren, alles unter Ausnutzung von YAML-Konfigurationsdateien wie experiment_summary.yaml.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar tramas HTML interativas usando inspect-viz, inferir tipos de visualização a partir de variáveis experimentais e registrar processos em arquivos de log, tudo isso aproveitando arquivos de configuração YAML como experiment_summary.yaml.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать интерактивные HTML-плоты с помощью inspect-viz, выводить типы визуализации из экспериментальных переменных и регистрировать процессы в журналах, все это при помощи файлов конфигурации YAML, таких как experiment_summary.yaml.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من توليد رسومات HTML التفاعلية باستخدام inspect-viz، وافتراض أنواع التصور من المتغيرات التجريبية، وتسجيل العمليات في سجلات، كل ذلك بالاستفادة من ملفات التكوين YAML مثل experiment_summary.yaml."},"useCases":{"en":["Visualizing evaluation results from completed experiments","Generating interactive HTML and PNG plots for experimental data","Inferring appropriate visualization types based on experimental variables"],"zh":["可视化已完成实验的评估结果","生成交互式HTML和PNG绘图用于实验数据","根据实验变量推断适当的可视化类型"],"ja":["完了した実験の評価結果を視覚化する","実験データ用のインタラクティブなHTMLおよびPNGプロットを生成する","実験変数に基づいて適切な視覚化タイプを推測する"],"ko":["완료된 실험의 평가 결과를 시각화하는 것","실험 데이터를 위한 상호작용형 HTML 및 PNG 플롯을 생성하는 것","실험 변수를 기반으로 적절한 시각화 유형을 추론하는 것"],"es":["Visualizar resultados de evaluación de experimentos completados","Generar tramas HTML y PNG interactivas para datos experimentales","Inferir tipos de visualización adecuados en función de variables experimentales"],"fr":["Visualiser les résultats d''évaluation d''expériences terminées","Générer des trames HTML et PNG interactives pour des données expérimentales","Inférer des types de visualisation appropriés en fonction de variables expérimentales"],"de":["Visualisieren von Bewertungsergebnissen abgeschlossener Experimente","Generieren interaktiver HTML- und PNG-Plots für experimentelle Daten","Ableiten geeigneter Visualisierungstypen basierend auf experimentellen Variablen"],"pt":["Visualizar resultados de avaliação de experimentos concluídos","Gerar tramas HTML e PNG interativas para dados experimentais","Inferir tipos de visualização apropriados com base em variáveis experimentais"],"ru":["Визуализация результатов оценки завершенных экспериментов","Генерация интерактивных HTML- и PNG-плот для экспериментальных данных","Вывод подходящих типов визуализации на основе экспериментальных переменных"],"ar":["تصور نتائج التقييم من التجارب المكتملة","توليد رسومات HTML و PNG التفاعلية للبيانات التجريبية","افتراض أنواع التصور المناسبة بناءً على المتغيرات التجريبية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires experiment_summary.yaml for experimental design understanding","Needs access to run directories for evaluation logs","Dependent on inspect-viz for plot generation"],"zh":["需要experiment_summary.yaml来理解实验设计","需要访问运行目录以获取评估日志","依赖于inspect-viz来生成绘图"],"ja":["実験設計を理解するためにexperiment_summary.yamlが必要","評価ログを取得するために実行ディレクトリへのアクセスが必要","プロットの生成にinspect-vizに依存する"],"ko":["실험 설계를 이해하기 위해 experiment_summary.yaml가 필요함","평가 로그를 얻기 위해 실행 디렉토리에 대한 액세스가 필요함","플롯 생성에 대해 inspect-viz에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere experiment_summary.yaml para la comprensión del diseño experimental","Necesita acceso a directorios de ejecución para registros de evaluación","Depende de inspect-viz para la generación de tramas"],"fr":["Nécessite experiment_summary.yaml pour la compréhension de la conception expérimentale","A besoin d''un accès aux répertoires d''exécution pour les journaux d''évaluation","Dépend de inspect-viz pour la génération de trames"],"de":["Benötigt experiment_summary.yaml für das Verständnis des experimentellen Designs","Benötigt Zugriff auf Ausführungsverzeichnisse für Bewertungsprotokolle","Abhängig von inspect-viz für die Plotgenerierung"],"pt":["Requer experiment_summary.yaml para compreensão do design experimental","Necessita acesso a diretórios de execução para logs de avaliação","Dependente de inspect-viz para geração de tramas"],"ru":["Требует experiment_summary.yaml для понимания экспериментального дизайна","Требует доступа к директориям запуска для логов оценки","Зависит от inspect-viz для генерации плот"],"ar":["يتطلب experiment_summary.yaml لفهم تصميم التجربة","يحتاج الوصول إلى دليل التشغيل لتسجيلات التقييم","يعتمد على inspect-viz لتوليد الرسومات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"67f892cf98d08b22b5976c7d2fca6e3d71b6689edb77b0e8484a47e1fc98e3a9","qualityScore":52}');
