guration de cursor"],"de":["KI-Agent-Tools","KI-Framework","wie man KI-Agents verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu Claude Code","Installationsanleitung für Codex","Cursor-Konfiguration"],"pt":["como usar start framework","AI Agents TypeScript","CLI para desenvolvimento IA","start vs cursor comparison","instalar start framework","workflow automação coding","ferramentas developer AI","setup start typescript"],"ru":["как использовать start фреймворк","ИИ Агенты TypeScript","CLI для разработки ИИ","start vs cursor сравнение","установить start framework","workflow автоматизация кодирования","инструменты developer AI","настройка start typescript"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام إطار عمل start","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي TypeScript","واجهة سطر أوامر لتطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","مقارنة start مقابل cursor","تثبيت إطار عمل start","أتمتة سير عمل البرمجة","أدوات مطوري الذكاء الاصطناعي","إعداد start typescript"]}},"owner":"mindfold-ai","repo":"Trellis","repoPath":"mindfold-ai/Trellis","stars":2875,"forks":149,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T01:53:07Z","topics":["ai-agent","ai-coding","claude-code","cli","codex","cursor","developer-tools","typescript","workflow"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"start","description":"Start Session","bodyPreview":"# Start Session\n\nInitialize your AI development session and begin working on tasks.\n\n---\n\n## Operation Types\n\n| Marker | Meaning | Executor |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| `[AI]` | Bash scripts or tool calls executed by AI | You (AI) |\n| `[USER]` | Skills executed by user | User |\n\n---\n\n## Initialization `[AI]`\n\n### Step 1: Understand Development Workflow\n\nFirst, read the workflow guide to understand the development process:\n\n```bash\ncat .trellis/workflow.md\n```\n\n**Follow the instructions in","body":"# Start Session\n\nInitialize your AI development session and begin working on tasks.\n\n---\n\n## Operation Types\n\n| Marker | Meaning | Executor |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| `[AI]` | Bash scripts or tool calls executed by AI | You (AI) |\n| `[USER]` | Skills executed by user | User |\n\n---\n\n## Initialization `[AI]`\n\n### Step 1: Understand Development Workflow\n\nFirst, read the workflow guide to understand the development process:\n\n```bash\ncat .trellis/workflow.md\n```\n\n**Follow the instructions in workflow.md** - it contains:\n- Core principles (Read Before Write, Follow Standards, etc.)\n- File system structure\n- Development process\n- Best practices\n\n### Step 2: Get Current Context\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py\n```\n\nThis shows: developer identity, git status, current task (if any), active tasks.\n\n### Step 3: Read Guidelines Index\n\n```bash\ncat .trellis/spec/frontend/index.md  # Frontend guidelines\ncat .trellis/spec/backend/index.md   # Backend guidelines\ncat .trellis/spec/guides/index.md    # Thinking guides\n```\n\n### Step 4: Report and Ask\n\nReport what you learned and ask: \"What would you like to work on?\"\n\n---\n\n## Task Classification\n\nWhen user describes a task, classify it:\n\n| Type | Criteria | Workflow |\n|------|----------|----------|\n| **Question** | User asks about code, architecture, or how something works | Answer directly |\n| **Trivial Fix** | Typo fix, comment update, single-line change, < 5 minutes | Direct Edit |\n| **Simple Task** | Clear goal, 1-2 files, well-defined scope | Quick confirm → Task Workflow |\n| **Complex Task** | Vague goal, multiple files, architectural decisions | **Brainstorm → Task Workflow** |\n\n### Decision Rule\n\n> **If in doubt, use Brainstorm + Task Workflow.**\n>\n> Task Workflow ensures code-specs are injected to the right context, resulting in higher quality code.\n> The overhead is minimal, but the benefit is significant.\n\n---\n\n## Question / Trivial Fix\n\nFor questions or trivial fixes, work directly:\n\n1. Answer question or make the fix\n2. If code was changed, remind user to run `$finish-work`\n\n---\n\n## Simple Task\n\nFor simple, well-defined tasks:\n\n1. Quick confirm: \"I understand you want to [goal]. Ready to proceed?\"\n2. If yes, proceed to **Task Workflow Phase 1 Path B** (create task, write PRD, then research)\n3. If no, clarify and confirm again\n\n---\n\n## Complex Task - Brainstorm First\n\nFor complex or vague tasks, use the brainstorm process to clarify requirements.\n\nSee `$brainstorm` for the full process. Summary:\n\n1. **Acknowledge and classify** - State your understanding\n2. **Create task directory** - Track evolving requirements in `prd.md`\n3. **Ask questions one at a time** - Update PRD after each answer\n4. **Propose approaches** - For architectural decisions\n5. **Confirm final requirements** - Get explicit approval\n6. **Proceed to Task Workflow** - With clear requirements in PRD\n\n---\n\n## Task Workflow (Development Tasks)\n\n**Why this workflow?**\n- Run a dedicated research pass before coding\n- Configure specs in jsonl context files\n- Implement using injected context\n- Verify with a separate check pass\n- Result: Code that follows project conventions automatically\n\n### Overview: Two Entry Points\n\n```\nFrom Brainstorm (Complex Task):\n  PRD confirmed → Research → Configure Context → Activate → Implement → Check → Complete\n\nFrom Simple Task:\n  Confirm → Create Task → Write PRD → Research → Configure Context → Activate → Implement → Check → Complete\n```\n\n**Key principle: Research happens AFTER requirements are clear (PRD exists).**\n\n---\n\n### Phase 1: Establish Requirements\n\n#### Path A: From Brainstorm (skip to Phase 2)\n\nPRD and task directory already exist from brainstorm. Skip directly to Phase 2.\n\n#### Path B: From Simple Task\n\n**Step 1: Confirm Understanding** `[AI]`\n\nQuick confirm:\n- What is the goal?\n- What type of development? (frontend / backend / fullstack)\n- Any specific requirements or constraints?\n\nIf unclear, ask clarifying questions.\n\n**Step 2: Create Task Directory** `[AI]`\n\n```bash\nTASK_DIR=$(python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create \"<title>\" --slug <name>)\n```\n\n**Step 3: Write PRD** `[AI]`\n\nCreate `prd.md` in the task directory with:\n\n```markdown\n# <Task Title>\n\n## Goal\n<What we''re trying to achieve>\n\n## Requirements\n- <Requirement 1>\n- <Requirement 2>\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] <Criterion 1>\n- [ ] <Criterion 2>\n\n## Technical Notes\n<Any technical decisions or constraints>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Prepare for Implementation (shared)\n\n> Both paths converge here. PRD and task directory must exist before proceeding.\n\n**Step 4: Code-Spec Depth Check** `[AI]`\n\nIf the task touches infra or cross-layer contracts, do not start implementation until code-spec depth is defined.\n\nTrigger this requirement when the change includes any of:\n- New or changed command/API signatures\n- Database schema or migration changes\n- Infra integrations (storage, queue, cache, secrets, env contracts)\n- Cross-layer payload transformations\n\nMust-have before proceeding:\n- [ ] Target code-spec files to update are identified\n- [ ] Concrete contract is defined (signature, fields, env keys)\n- [ ] Validation and error matrix is defined\n- [ ] At least one Good/Base/Bad case is defined\n\n**Step 5: Research the Codebase** `[AI]`\n\nBased on the confirmed PRD, run a focused research pass and produce:\n\n1. Relevant spec files in `.trellis/spec/`\n2. Existing code patterns to follow (2-3 examples)\n3. Files that will likely need modification\n\nUse this output format:\n\n```markdown\n## Relevant Specs\n- <path>: <why it''s relevant>\n\n## Code Patterns Found\n- <pattern>: <example file path>\n\n## Files to Modify\n- <path>: <what change>\n```\n\n**Step 6: Configure Context** `[AI]`\n\nInitialize default context:\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py init-context \"$TASK_DIR\" <type>\n# type: backend | frontend | fullstack\n```\n\nAdd specs found in your research pass:\n\n```bash\n# For each relevant spec and code pattern:\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-context \"$TASK_DIR\" implement \"<path>\" \"<reason>\"\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-context \"$TASK_DIR\" check \"<path>\" \"<reason>\"\n```\n\n**Step 7: Activate Task** `[AI]`\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py start \"$TASK_DIR\"\n```\n\nThis sets `.current-task` so hooks can inject context.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Execute (shared)\n\n**Step 8: Implement** `[AI]`\n\nImplement the task described in `prd.md`.\n\n- Follow all specs injected into implement context\n- Keep changes scoped to requirements\n- Run lint and typecheck before finishing\n\n**Step 9: Check Quality** `[AI]`\n\nRun a quality pass against check context:\n\n- Review all code changes against the specs\n- Fix issues directly\n- Ensure lint and typecheck pass\n\n**Step 10: Complete** `[AI]`\n\n1. Verify lint and typecheck pass\n2. Report what was implemented\n3. Remind user to:\n   - Test the changes\n   - Commit when ready\n   - Run `$record-session` to record this session\n\n---\n\n## Continuing Existing Task\n\nIf `get_context.py` shows a current task:\n\n1. Read the task''s `prd.md` to understand the goal\n2. Check `task.json` for current status and phase\n3. Ask user: \"Continue working on <task-name>?\"\n\nIf yes, resume from the appropriate step (usually Step 7 or 8).\n\n---\n\n## Skills Reference\n\n### User Skills `[USER]`\n\n| Skill | When to Use |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `$start` | Begin a session (this skill) |\n| `$finish-work` | Before committing changes |\n| `$record-session` | After completing a task |\n\n### AI Scripts `[AI]`\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py` | Get session context |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create` | Create task directory |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py init-context` | Initialize jsonl files |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-context` | Add spec to jsonl |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py start` | Set current task |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py finish` | Clear current task |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py archive` | Archive completed task |\n\n### Workflow Phases `[AI]`\n\n| Phase | Purpose | Context Source |\n|-------|---------|----------------|\n| research | Analyze codebase | direct repo inspection |\n| implement | Write code | `implement.jsonl` |\n| check | Review & fix | `check.jsonl` |\n| debug | Fix specific issues | `debug.jsonl` |\n\n---\n\n## Key Principle\n\n> **Code-spec context is injected, not remembered.**\n>\n> The Task Workflow ensures agents receive relevant code-spec context automatically.\n> This is more reliable than hoping the AI \"remembers\" conventions.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T02:13:34.759Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing streamlined workflow initialization and task management.","zh":"非常适合需要简化工作流初始化和任务管理的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントがワークフローの初期化とタスク管理を効率化する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 워크플로우 초기화와 작업 관리를 간소화해야 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una inicialización de flujo de trabajo y gestión de tareas simplificadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant une initialisation de workflow et une gestion de tâches rationalisées.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine gestreamte Workflow-Initialisierung und Aufgabenverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de inicialização de fluxo de trabalho simplificado e gerenciamento de tarefas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходима упрощенная инициализация рабочего процесса и управление задачами.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى تهيئة تدفق العمل المُبسطة وتحكم المهام."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initialize development sessions, execute Bash scripts, and interact with workflow guides using Markdown files, providing a comprehensive development framework.","zh":"赋予代理初始化开发会话、执行Bash脚本和使用Markdown文件与工作流指南交互的能力，提供了一个全面的开发框架。","ja":"開発エージェントが開発セッションを初期化し、Bashスクリプトを実行し、Markdownファイルを使用してワークフローガイドとやり取りできるようにし、包括的な開発フレームワークを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 개발 세션을 초기화하고 Bash 스크립트를 실행하며 Markdown 파일을 사용하여 워크플로우 가이드와 상호 작용할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 종합적인 개발 프레임워크를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a inicializar sesiones de desarrollo, ejecutar scripts de Bash y interactuar con guías de flujo de trabajo utilizando archivos Markdown, proporcionando un marco de desarrollo integral que incluye React, Python, CLI y API.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''initialiser des sessions de développement, d''exécuter des scripts Bash et d''interagir avec des guides de workflow à l''aide de fichiers Markdown, fournissant un cadre de développement complet qui inclut React, Python, CLI et API.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Entwicklungssitzungen zu initialisieren, Bash-Skripte auszuführen und mit Workflow-Leitfäden über Markdown-Dateien zu interagieren, wodurch ein umfassendes Entwicklungsframework bereitgestellt wird, das React, Python, CLI und API umfasst.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a inicializar sessões de desenvolvimento, executar scripts Bash e interagir com guias de fluxo de trabalho usando arquivos Markdown, fornecendo uma estrutura de desenvolvimento abrangente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью инициализации сессий разработки, выполнения скриптов Bash и взаимодействия с рабочими руководствами с использованием файлов Markdown, обеспечивая комплексную разработочную структуру.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تهيئة جلسات التطوير وتشغيل سكريبتات Bash والتفاعل مع دلائل التدفق العمل باستخدام ملفات Markdown، مما يوفر إطارًا شاملاً للتنمية."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing AI development sessions","Executing Bash scripts for workflow automation","Parsing Markdown guides for development workflow"],"zh":["初始化AI开发会话","执行Bash脚本以实现工作流自动化","解析Markdown指南以用于开发工作流"],"ja":["AI開発セッションの初期化","ワークフロー自動化のためのBashスクリプトの実行","開発ワークフローに使用するためのMarkdownガイドの解析"],"ko":["AI 개발 세션 초기화","워크플로우 자동화를 위한 Bash 스크립트 실행","개발 워크플로우에 사용되는 Markdown 가이드 파싱"],"es":["Inicialización de sesiones de desarrollo de IA","Ejecución de scripts de Bash para la automatización del flujo de trabajo","Análisis de guías de Markdown para el flujo de trabajo de desarrollo"],"fr":["Initialisation de sessions de développement d''IA","Exécution de scripts Bash pour l''automatisation du workflow","Analyse de guides Markdown pour le workflow de développement"],"de":["Initialisierung von AI-Entwicklungssitzungen","Ausführung von Bash-Skripten für die Workflow-Automatisierung","Analyse von Markdown-Leitfäden für den Entwicklungswerkfluss"],"pt":["Inicializando sessões de desenvolvimento de IA","Executando scripts Bash para automação de fluxo de trabalho","Analysando guias Markdown para fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Инициализация сессий разработки ИИ","Выполнение скриптов Bash для автоматизации рабочего процесса","Парсинг руководств Markdown для рабочего процесса разработки"],"ar":["تهيئة جلسات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","تشغيل سكريبتات Bash للتحكم الآلي في تدفق العمل","تحليل دلائل Markdown لتدفق عمل التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to .trellis/workflow.md file","Bash script execution capabilities needed"],"zh":["需要访问.trellis/workflow.md文件","需要Bash脚本执行能力"],"ja":[".trellis/workflow.mdファイルへのアクセスが必要","Bashスクリプトの実行機能が必要"],"ko":[".trellis/workflow.md 파일에 접근할 수 있어야 합니다","Bash 스크립트 실행 기능이 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso al archivo .trellis/workflow.md","Se necesitan capacidades de ejecución de scripts de Bash"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès au fichier .trellis/workflow.md","Des capacités d''exécution de scripts Bash sont nécessaires"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Datei .trellis/workflow.md","Bash-Skript-Ausführungsfähigkeiten sind erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arquivo .trellis/workflow.md","Capacidades de execução de scripts Bash necessárias"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к файлу .trellis/workflow.md","Необходимы возможности выполнения скриптов Bash"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الملف .trellis/workflow.md","يحتاج إلى إمكانيات تشغيل سكريبتات Bash"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"6ab8be66e77e5b13845bcf0610df8c12cebca1dc802f2f5d47562177be991ffb","qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('pgplex/pgschema/fix_bug', 'community', 'pgplex', 'pgschema', 'pgplex/pgschema', 'fix_bug', 808, 30, 50, '2026-03-01T03:56:36Z', '2026-03-01T12:48:22.838Z', '3405298c5aac79ae318b9dcdd0980d9642d596874ccb536084cf31e8c3d33399', '{"id":"pgplex/pgschema/fix_bug","name":"fix_bug","description":{"zh":"fix_bug是Postgres数据库的Terraform风格的声明式schema迁移CLI工具，用于简化数据库schema的管理","ja":"fix_bugはPostgresデータベースのTerraformスタイルの宣言的なスキーマ移行CLIツールであり、データベーススキーマの管理を簡素化するために使用されます","ko":"fix_bug는 Postgres 데이터베이스의 테라폼 스타일의 선언적 스키마 마이그레이션 CLI 도구로서 데이터베이스 스키마의 관리를 간소화하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"Fix Bug es una herramienta de migración de esquema declarativa para Postgres, similar a Terraform, que permite la gestión de cambios de esquema de manera eficiente","fr":"Fix Bug est un outil de migration de schéma déclaratif pour Postgres, similaire à Terraform, qui permet la gestion des changements de schéma de manière efficace","de":"Fix Bug ist ein deklaratives Schema-Migrations-Tool für Postgres, ähnlich wie Terraform, das die Verwaltung von Schema-Änderungen auf effiziente Weise ermöglicht","pt":"A ferramenta fix_bug é uma CLI de migração de esquema declarativa estilo Terraform para Postgres, facilitando a gestão de esquemas de banco de dados.","ru":"Инструмент fix_bug - это декларативный CLI для миграции схемы Postgres в стиле Terraform, упрощающий управление схемами базы данных.","ar":"أداة fix_bug هي أداة سطر أوامر لمخطط قاعدة البيانات Postgres بطريقة Terraform، تسهل إدارة مخططات قاعدة البيانات.","en":"Terraform-style, declarative schema migration CLI for Postgres"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AIエージェント：Postgres Terraform风格的声明式schema迁移CLI","ja":"AIエージェント：PostgresのTerraformスタイルの宣言的なスキーマ移行CLI","ko":"AI 에이전트: Postgres 테라폼 스타일의 선언적 스키마 마이그레이션 CLI","es":"Herramientas de agente de inteligencia artificial: Fix Bu...","fr":"Outils d''agent d''intelligence artificielle: Fix Bug CLI","de":"KI-Agents-Tools: Fix Bug CLI","pt":"Ferramenta de Migração de Esquema Postgres - Ferramentas ...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Инструмент Миграции Схемы Postgres","ar":"أداة إدارة مخطط القاعدةPostgres - أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"fix_bug"},"description":{"zh":"fix_bug是Postgres数据库的Terraform风格的声明式schema迁移CLI工具，用于简化数据库schema的管理","ja":"fix_bugはPostgresデータベースのTerraformスタイルの宣言的なスキーマ移行CLIツールであり、データベーススキーマの管理を簡素化するために使用されます","ko":"fix_bug는 Postgres 데이터베이스의 테라폼 스타일의 선언적 스키마 마이그레이션 CLI 도구로서 데이터베이스 스키마의 관리를 간소화하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"Fix Bug es una herramienta de migración de esquema declarativa para Postgres, similar a Terraform, que permite la gestión de cambios de esquema de manera efi...","fr":"Fix Bug est un outil de migration de schéma déclaratif pour Postgres, similaire à Terraform, qui permet la gestion des changements de schéma de manière efficace","de":"Fix Bug ist ein deklaratives Schema-Migrations-Tool für Postgres, ähnlich wie Terraform, das die Verwaltung von Schema-Änderungen auf effiziente Weise ermögl...","pt":"A ferramenta fix_bug é uma CLI de migração de esquema declarativa estilo Terraform para Postgres, facilitando a gestão de esquemas de banco de dados.","ru":"Инструмент fix_bug - это декларативный CLI для миграции схемы Postgres в стиле Terraform, упрощающий управление схемами базы данных.","ar":"أداة fix_bug هي أداة سطر أوامر لمخطط قاعدة البيانات Postgres بطريقة Terraform، تسهل إدارة مخططات قاعدة البيانات.","en":"Terraform-style, declarative schema migration CLI for Postgres"},"definition":{"en":"Terraform-style, declarative schema migration CLI for Postgres"},"features":{"zh":["Terraform风格的声明式schema迁移","Postgres数据库支持","CLI工具，易于使用","多租户支持","GitOps集成"],"ja":["Terraformスタイルの宣言的なスキーマ移行","Postgresデータベース対応","CLIツール、使いやすい","マルチテナント対応","GitOps統合"],"ko":["테라폼 스타일의 선언적 스키마 마이그레이션","Postgres 데이터베이스 지원","CLI 도구, 사용하기 쉽습니다","멀티 테넌트 지원","GitOps 통합"],"es":["Migración de esquema declarativa para Postgres","Similar a Terraform","Gestión de cambios de esquema eficiente","Compatible con CI/CD y GitOps","Soporte para entornos multi-tenant"],"fr":["Migration de schéma déclaratif pour Postgres","Similaire à Terraform","Gestion des changements de schéma efficace","Compatible avec CI/CD et GitOps","Support pour les environnements multi-locataires"],"de":["Deklarative Schema-Migration für Postgres","Ähnlich wie Terraform","Effiziente Verwaltung von Schema-Änderungen","Kompatibel mit CI/CD und GitOps","Unterstützung für Multi-Tenant-Umgebungen"],"pt":["Migração de esquema declarativa","CLI estilo Terraform","Suporte a Postgres","Gestão de esquemas de banco de dados","Integração com CI/CD"],"ru":["Декларативная миграция схемы","CLI в стиле Terraform","Поддержка Postgres","Управление схемами базы данных","Интеграция с CI/CD"],"ar":["هجرة مخطط إعلاني","سطر أوامر بطريقة Terraform","دعم Postgres","إدارة مخططات قاعدة البيانات","التكامل مع CI/CD"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Postgres schema迁移","Terraform风格的schema管理","fix_bug工具","数据库schema管理","GitOps集成","多租户支持","CLI工具","如何使用fix_bug","fix_bug安装"],"ja":["Postgresスキーマ移行","Terraformスタイルのスキーマ管理","fix_bugツール","データベーススキーマ管理","GitOps統合","マルチテナント対応","CLIツール","fix_bugの使用方法","fix_bugのインストール"],"ko":["Postgres 스키마 마이그레이션","테라폼 스타일의 스키마 관리","fix_bug 도구","데이터베이스 스키마 관리","GitOps 통합","멀티 테넌트 지원","CLI 도구","fix_bug 사용 방법","fix_bug 설치"],"es":["cómo usar Fix Bug","qué es la migración de esquema","alternativas a Fix Bug","Fix Bug vs Terraform","instalación de Fix Bug","guía de configuración de Fix Bug","herramientas de agente de inteligencia artificial","migración de esquema declarativa","gestión de cambios de esquema"],"fr":["comment utiliser Fix Bug","quoi est la migration de schéma","alternatives à Fix Bug","Fix Bug vs Terraform","installation de Fix Bug","guide de configuration de Fix Bug","outils d''agent d''intelligence artificielle","migration de schéma déclaratif","gestion des changements de schéma"],"de":["wie man Fix Bug verwendet","was ist Schema-Migration","Alternativen zu Fix Bug","Fix Bug vs Terraform","Installation von Fix Bug","Konfigurationsanleitung für Fix Bug","KI-Agents-Tools","deklarative Schema-Migration","Verwaltung von Schema-Änderungen"],"pt":["ferramenta de migração de esquema","como usar fix_bug","o que é migração de esquema","fix_bug vs outras ferramentas","instalar fix_bug","guia de configuração do fix_bug","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["инструмент миграции схемы","как использовать fix_bug","что такое миграция схемы","fix_bug vs другие инструменты","установить fix_bug","руководство по настройке fix_bug","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков"],"ar":["أداة إدارة مخطط قاعدة البيانات","كيفية استخدام fix_bug","ما هي هجرة مخطط قاعدة البيانات","fix_bug مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت fix_bug","دليل إعداد fix_bug","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين"]}},"owner":"pgplex","repo":"pgschema","repoPath":"pgplex/pgschema","stars":808,"forks":30,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T03:56:36Z","topics":["cicd","cli","ddl","devops","gitops","multi-tenant","postgres","postgresql","schema","schema-change","schema-diff","schema-migration","schema-migrations","terraform"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fix_bug","description":"Fix a bug from a GitHub issue using TDD. Analyzes the issue, creates a reproducing test case, implements the fix, verifies it, runs refactor-pass, and creates a PR.","bodyPreview":"# Fix Bug\n\nEnd-to-end workflow for fixing bugs reported as GitHub issues. Uses TDD: reproduce first, then fix, then verify.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- A GitHub issue URL or issue number (from the pgplex/pgschema repo)\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Analyze the Issue\n\n1. **Fetch the issue** using `gh issue view <number>` to get the full description, labels, and any linked PRs.\n2. **Understand the bug**: Identify what''s broken, what the expected behavior is, and which area of code is affected.\n3. **Classify","body":"# Fix Bug\n\nEnd-to-end workflow for fixing bugs reported as GitHub issues. Uses TDD: reproduce first, then fix, then verify.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- A GitHub issue URL or issue number (from the pgplex/pgschema repo)\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Analyze the Issue\n\n1. **Fetch the issue** using `gh issue view <number>` to get the full description, labels, and any linked PRs.\n2. **Understand the bug**: Identify what''s broken, what the expected behavior is, and which area of code is affected.\n3. **Classify the bug type**:\n   - **Dump bug**: `pgschema dump` produces incorrect output (wrong SQL, missing objects, bad formatting). Test goes in `testdata/dump/`.\n   - **Diff/Plan bug**: `pgschema dump` is correct but `pgschema plan` generates wrong migration DDL. Test goes in `testdata/diff/`.\n   - **Both**: If unclear, start with dump. If dump output is correct, it''s a diff bug.\n\n### Phase 2: Create the Test Case (TDD - Red)\n\n#### For Dump Bugs (`testdata/dump/`)\n\n1. **Create test directory**:\n   ```\n   testdata/dump/issue_<NUMBER>_<short_description>/\n   ```\n   Use snake_case for the description. Example: `issue_250_enum_type_missing`\n\n2. **Create test files**:\n   - `manifest.json` - Metadata about the test case:\n     ```json\n     {\n       \"name\": \"issue_<NUMBER>_<short_description>\",\n       \"description\": \"Test case for <bug description> (GitHub issue #<NUMBER>)\",\n       \"source\": \"https://github.com/pgplex/pgschema/issues/<NUMBER>\",\n       \"notes\": [\n         \"Reproduces the bug where <specific behavior>\",\n         \"Tests that <expected correct behavior>\"\n       ]\n     }\n     ```\n   - `raw.sql` - The original DDL that creates the schema (what a user would write)\n   - `pgdump.sql` - What `pg_dump --schema-only` produces for this schema (the input to the test). Generate this by applying `raw.sql` to an embedded-postgres and running pg_dump, or construct it manually based on pg_dump conventions.\n   - `pgschema.sql` - The expected correct output from `pgschema dump`\n\n3. **Register the test** in `cmd/dump/dump_integration_test.go`:\n   ```go\n   func TestDumpCommand_Issue<NUMBER><PascalDescription>(t *testing.T) {\n       if testing.Short() {\n           t.Skip(\"Skipping integration test in short mode\")\n       }\n       runExactMatchTest(t, \"issue_<NUMBER>_<short_description>\")\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Run the test to confirm it fails** (red):\n   ```bash\n   go test -v ./cmd/dump -run TestDumpCommand_Issue<NUMBER>\n   ```\n\n#### For Diff/Plan Bugs (`testdata/diff/`)\n\n1. **Create test directory** under the appropriate category:\n   ```\n   testdata/diff/<category>/issue_<NUMBER>_<short_description>/\n   ```\n   Categories: `create_table`, `create_index`, `create_trigger`, `create_view`, `create_function`, `create_procedure`, `create_sequence`, `create_type`, `create_domain`, `create_policy`, `create_materialized_view`, `comment`, `privilege`, `default_privilege`, `dependency`, `online`, `migrate`.\n\n   Example: `testdata/diff/create_index/issue_250_partial_index_diff`\n\n2. **Create test files**:\n   - `old.sql` - The starting schema state (current database)\n   - `new.sql` - The desired schema state (user''s SQL files)\n   - Leave `diff.sql` empty or with expected content — it will be generated\n   - Note: `plan.json`, `plan.sql`, `plan.txt` will also be generated alongside `diff.sql`\n\n3. **Run the diff test to confirm it fails** (red):\n   ```bash\n   PGSCHEMA_TEST_FILTER=\"<category>/issue_<NUMBER>_<short_description>\" go test -v ./internal/diff -run TestDiffFromFiles\n   ```\n\n4. **Generate expected outputs** using `--generate` once you know the correct behavior:\n   ```bash\n   PGSCHEMA_TEST_FILTER=\"<category>/issue_<NUMBER>_<short_description>\" go test -v ./cmd -run TestPlanAndApply --generate\n   ```\n   This overwrites `diff.sql`, `plan.json`, `plan.sql`, and `plan.txt` with actual output.\n\n### Phase 3: Implement the Fix (Green)\n\n1. **Locate the relevant code**. Common locations:\n   - Dump bugs: `ir/inspector.go` (database introspection), `ir/normalize.go` (normalization), `internal/dump/` (output formatting)\n   - Diff bugs: `internal/diff/` (comparison logic — `table.go`, `column.go`, `index.go`, `trigger.go`, `view.go`, `function.go`, `procedure.go`, `sequence.go`, `type.go`, `policy.go`, `constraint.go`)\n   - IR bugs: `ir/ir.go` (data structures), `ir/quote.go` (identifier quoting)\n\n2. **Use reference skills as needed**:\n   - Consult **pg_dump Reference** skill for correct system catalog queries\n   - Consult **PostgreSQL Syntax Reference** skill for grammar questions\n   - Use **Validate with Database** skill to test queries against live PostgreSQL\n\n3. **Make the minimal fix**. Do not refactor surrounding code — focus on the bug.\n\n4. **Run the test to confirm it passes** (green):\n   ```bash\n   # For dump bugs\n   go test -v ./cmd/dump -run TestDumpCommand_Issue<NUMBER>\n\n   # For diff bugs\n   PGSCHEMA_TEST_FILTER=\"<category>/issue_<NUMBER>\" go test -v ./internal/diff -run TestDiffFromFiles\n   PGSCHEMA_TEST_FILTER=\"<category>/issue_<NUMBER>\" go test -v ./cmd -run TestPlanAndApply\n   ```\n\n### Phase 4: Verify No Regressions\n\nRun related tests selectively to verify nothing in the affected area broke. Do NOT run the full test suite (`go test -v ./...`) locally — it often times out due to resource constraints. The full regression suite runs in GitHub CI after the PR is created.\n\n```bash\n# For dump bugs — run the dump test suite\ngo test -v ./cmd/dump\n\n# For diff bugs — run tests in the same category\nPGSCHEMA_TEST_FILTER=\"<category>/\" go test -v ./internal/diff -run TestDiffFromFiles\nPGSCHEMA_TEST_FILTER=\"<category>/\" go test -v ./cmd -run TestPlanAndApply\n```\n\nIf any related tests fail, investigate and fix before proceeding.\n\n### Phase 5: Refactor Pass\n\nInvoke the **refactor-pass** skill to clean up:\n- Remove any dead code introduced or exposed by the fix\n- Simplify logic if the fix revealed unnecessary complexity\n- Ensure the test case is clean and minimal\n- Run build/tests to verify behavior after cleanup\n\n### Phase 6: Create PR\n\n1. **Create a feature branch**:\n   ```bash\n   git checkout -b fix/issue-<NUMBER>-<short-description>\n   ```\n\n2. **Commit the changes** with a descriptive message:\n   ```\n   fix: <concise description of what was fixed> (#<NUMBER>)\n   ```\n\n3. **Push and create PR**:\n   ```bash\n   git push -u origin fix/issue-<NUMBER>-<short-description>\n   gh pr create --title \"fix: <description> (#<NUMBER>)\" --body \"...\"\n   ```\n\n   PR body should include:\n   - `## Summary` — What was broken and how it was fixed\n   - `Fixes #<NUMBER>` — Link to the issue for auto-close\n   - `## Test plan` — What test case was added and how to run it\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Issue analyzed and bug type classified (dump vs diff)\n- [ ] Test case created with proper naming (`issue_<NUMBER>_<description>`)\n- [ ] Test fails before fix (red)\n- [ ] Minimal fix implemented\n- [ ] Test passes after fix (green)\n- [ ] Related tests pass (no regressions in affected area; full suite runs in CI)\n- [ ] Refactor pass completed\n- [ ] PR created and linked to issue\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T12:48:22.838Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing end-to-end bug fixing workflows with GitHub issue integration and Test-Driven Development (TDD) capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要端到端 bug 修复工作流的开发代理，具有 GitHub 问题集成和测试驱动开发（TDD）能力。","ja":"開発エージェントが GitHub の問題を統合し、テスト駆動開発（TDD）能力を持つエンドツーエンドのバグ修正ワークフローを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"GitHub 이슈 통합 및 테스트 주도 개발(TDD) 기능을 갖춘 엔드 투 엔드 버그 수정 워크플로가 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan flujos de trabajo de solución de errores de extremo a extremo con integración de problemas de GitHub y capacidades de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD).","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement ayant besoin de flux de travail de correction de bogues de bout en bout avec une intégration des problèmes GitHub et des capacités de Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD).","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel benötigende Entwicklungsagenten mit End-to-End-Fehlerbehebungsworkflows und GitHub-Issue-Integration sowie Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD)-Fähigkeiten.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de fluxos de trabalho de correção de bugs de ponta a ponta com integração de issues do GitHub e capacidades de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD).","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуются конечные рабочие процессы исправления ошибок с интеграцией проблем GitHub и возможностями разработки, управляемой тестированием (TDD).","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يحتاج إلى سير عمل إصلاح العيوب من النهاية إلى النهاية مع دمج مشكلة GitHub وخصائص التطوير الموجه بالأمر (TDD)."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to reproduce, fix, and verify bugs using Terraform-style declarative schema migration for Postgres, leveraging GitHub issues and TDD principles with tools like gh issue view.","zh":"赋予代理使用 Terraform 风格的声明式模式迁移（针对 Postgres），同时利用 GitHub 问题和 TDD 原则以及类似 gh issue view 的工具来重现、修复和验证 bug 的能力。","ja":"エージェントに、Terraform スタイルの宣言型スキーマ移行（Postgres 対応）を使用して、GitHub の問題や TDD 原則および gh issue view のようなツールを活用し、バグを再現、修正、検証する能力を付与します。","ko":"에이전트가 Terraform 스타일의 선언적 스키마 마이그레이션(포스트그레스에 대한)을 사용하여 GitHub 이슈와 TDD 원칙 및 gh 이슈 뷰와 같은 도구를 활용하여 버그를 재현, 수정 및 검증할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a reproducir, solucionar y verificar errores utilizando una migración de esquema declarativa de estilo Terraform para Postgres, aprovechando los principios de problemas de GitHub y TDD con herramientas como gh issue view.","fr":"Permet aux agents de reproduire, de corriger et de vérifier les bogues en utilisant une migration de schéma déclarative de style Terraform pour Postgres, en exploitant les problèmes GitHub et les principes TDD avec des outils comme gh issue view.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Fehler mit einer deklarativen Schema-Migration im Terraform-Stil für Postgres zu reproduzieren, zu beheben und zu überprüfen, indem es die GitHub-Probleme und TDD-Prinzipien mit Tools wie gh issue view nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reproduzir, corrigir e verificar bugs usando migração de esquema declarativa no estilo Terraform para Postgres, aproveitando problemas do GitHub e princípios TDD com ferramentas como gh issue view.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью воспроизводить, исправлять и проверять ошибки, используя декларативную миграцию схемы в стиле Terraform для Postgres, используя проблемы GitHub и принципы TDD с помощью инструментов, таких как gh issue view.","ar":"يمكّن الوكيل من إعادة إنتاج وتصحيح وتحديد العيوب باستخدام هجرة مخطط إعلاني على الطراز Terraform لبرنامج Postgres، والاستفادة من مشاكل GitHub ومبادئ TDD باستخدام أدوات مثل gh issue view."},"useCases":{"en":["Reproducing bugs reported on GitHub","Fixing and verifying issues using TDD","Analyzing and classifying bugs for efficient resolution"],"zh":["在 GitHub 上报告的 bug 를 재현하기","TDD 를 사용하여 문제를 수정 및 확인하기","버그를 효율적으로 해결하기 위해 분석 및 분류하기"],"ja":["GitHub に報告されたバグを再現する","TDD を使用して問題を修正および検証する","バグを効率的に解決するために分析および分類する"],"ko":["GitHub 에 보고된 버그를 재현하기","TDD 를 사용하여 문제를 수정 및 확인하기","버그를 효율적으로 해결하기 위해 분석 및 분류하기"],"es":["Reproducir errores informados en GitHub","Solucionar y verificar problemas utilizando TDD","Analizar y clasificar errores para una resolución eficiente"],"fr":["Reproduire les bogues signalés sur GitHub","Corriger et vérifier les problèmes en utilisant TDD","Analyser et classer les bogues pour une résolution efficace"],"de":["Fehler reproduzieren, die in GitHub gemeldet werden","Fehler mit TDD beheben und überprüfen","Fehler analysieren und klassifizieren, um eine effiziente Behebung zu ermöglichen"],"pt":["Reproduzir bugs relatados no GitHub","Corrigir e verificar problemas usando TDD","Analizar e classificar bugs para resolução eficiente"],"ru":["Воспроизводить ошибки, сообщенные на GitHub","Исправлять и проверять проблемы с помощью TDD","Анализировать и классифицировать ошибки для эффективного решения"],"ar":["إعادة إنتاج العيوب المبلغ عنها على GitHub","تصحيح وتحديد المشاكل باستخدام TDD","تحليل وتصنيف العيوب لتحقيق حل فعال"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub issue URL or issue number from the pgplex/pgschema repo","Postgres database only","Terraform-style schema migration CLI required"],"zh":["需要来自 pgplex/pgschema 库的 GitHub 问题 URL 或问题编号","仅限 Postgres 数据库","需要 Terraform 风格的模式迁移 CLI"],"ja":["pgplex/pgschema リポジトリからの GitHub の問題 URL または問題番号が必要","Postgres データベースのみ","Terraform スタイルのスキーマ移行 CLI が必要"],"ko":["pgplex/pgschema 리포지토리에서 GitHub 이슈 URL 또는 이슈 번호가 필요","포스트그레스 데이터베이스만 해당","테라폼 스타일의 스키마 마이그레이션 CLI가 필요"],"es":["Requiere una URL de problema de GitHub o número de problema del repositorio pgplex/pgschema","Solo base de datos Postgres","Se requiere una migración de esquema de estilo Terraform CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite une URL de problème GitHub ou un numéro de problème du référentiel pgplex/pgschema","Base de données Postgres uniquement","Une migration de schéma de style Terraform CLI est requise"],"de":["Benötigt eine GitHub-Problemm-URL oder eine Problemmnummer aus dem pgplex/pgschema-Repository","Nur Postgres-Datenbank","Eine Terraform-Stil-Schema-Migration-CLI ist erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer URL de problema do GitHub ou número de problema do repositório pgplex/pgschema","Banco de dados Postgres apenas","CLI de migração de esquema no estilo Terraform necessário"],"ru":["Требуется URL проблемы GitHub или номер проблемы из репозитория pgplex/pgschema","Только база данных Postgres","Требуется CLI миграции схемы в стиле Terraform"],"ar":["يتطلب رابط URL لمشكلة GitHub أو رقم المشكلة من مستودع pgplex/pgschema","قاعدة بيانات Postgres فقط","مطلوب CLI للهجرة المخطط على الطراز Terraform"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3405298c5aac79ae318b9dcdd0980d9642d596874ccb536084cf31e8c3d33399","qualityScore":50}');
