frases","Filtros y agregaciones","Campos almacenados","Resaltado de resultados","Compatibilidad con vectores y GPU"],"fr":["Recherche de texte complet avec BM25 et correspondance de phrases","Filtres et agrégations","Champs stockés","Mise en évidence des résultats","Compatibilité avec les vecteurs et le GPU"],"de":["Volltextsuche mit BM25 und Phrasenübereinstimmung","Filter und Aggregationen","Gespeicherte Felder","Hervorhebung der Ergebnisse","Kompatibilität mit Vektoren und GPU"],"pt":["API em Rust para busca em texto completo","CLI para operações de busca","Recursos de busca em frase e correspondência de termos","Filtros e agregações para resultados de busca","Realce de resultados de busca"],"ru":["API на Rust для полнотекстового поиска","CLI для операций поиска","Функции поиска фраз и соответствия терминов","Фильтры и агрегации для результатов поиска","Выделение результатов поиска"],"ar":["واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Rust للبحث النصي الكامل","واجهة سطر أوامر للعمليات البحثية","خصائص البحث بالجملة والتوافق المصطلحي","مرشحات وتجميعات لنتائج البحث","تأكيد نتائج البحث"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用 Searchlite","Searchlite 教程","全文搜索工具","Searchlite 安装","Searchlite 设置指南","Searchlite 与 Elasticsearch 比较"],"ja":["Searchlite の使い方","Searchlite チュートリアル","全文検索ツール","Searchlite インストール","Searchlite セットアップガイド","Searchlite と Elasticsearch の比較"],"ko":["Searchlite 사용법","Searchlite 튜토리얼","전체 텍스트 검색 도구","Searchlite 설치","Searchlite 설정 가이드","Searchlite 와 Elasticsearch 비교"],"es":["herramientas de búsqueda de errores","cómo usar Searchlite","qué es Searchlite","Searchlite alternativa","Searchlite vs Elasticsearch","instalar Searchlite","guía de configuración de Searchlite"],"fr":["outils de recherche de bogues","comment utiliser Searchlite","qu''est-ce que Searchlite","Searchlite alternative","Searchlite vs Elasticsearch","installer Searchlite","guide de configuration de Searchlite"],"de":["Fehler-Such-Tools","wie man Searchlite verwendet","was ist Searchlite","Searchlite-Alternative","Searchlite vs Elasticsearch","Searchlite installieren","Searchlite-Konfigurationshandbuch"],"pt":["como usar Searchlite","o que é Searchlite","Searchlite alternativa","Searchlite vs ElasticSearch","instalar Searchlite","guia de configuração do Searchlite","desenvolvimento de software com Searchlite","busca em texto completo com Rust"],"ru":["как использовать Searchlite","что такое Searchlite","Searchlite альтернатива","Searchlite vs ElasticSearch","установить Searchlite","руководство по настройке Searchlite","разработка программного обеспечения с Searchlite","полнотекстовый поиск с помощью Rust"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Searchlite","ما هو Searchlite","بديل Searchlite","Searchlite مقابل ElasticSearch","تثبيت Searchlite","دليل إعداد Searchlite","تطوير البرمجيات مع Searchlite","البحث النصي الكامل مع Rust"]}},"owner":"davidkelley","repo":"searchlite","repoPath":"davidkelley/searchlite","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-27T01:51:08.526Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bug-hunting","description":"Structured workflow for discovering, reproducing, and fixing bugs in Searchlite by inspecting real code paths (CLI/HTTP/core), validating durability invariants, and producing regression tests; use when investigating incorrect results, crashes, data loss risks, or “it sometimes fails” reports.","bodyPreview":"# Bug Hunting Workflow\n\n## Intent\n\nThis skill is for **finding real bugs in the implementation**, not guessing. It forces a discovery phase (build a mental model, reproduce, narrow scope) before making changes.\n\nYou must prioritize:\n\n1. correctness and durability\n2. clear reproduction\n3. minimal fix + regression test\n\n---\n\n## Non-negotiable rules\n\n- **No fix without a reproduction** (a failing test, a minimal repro program, or a deterministic HTTP/CLI script).\n- **No durability regressions**: do","body":"# Bug Hunting Workflow\n\n## Intent\n\nThis skill is for **finding real bugs in the implementation**, not guessing. It forces a discovery phase (build a mental model, reproduce, narrow scope) before making changes.\n\nYou must prioritize:\n\n1. correctness and durability\n2. clear reproduction\n3. minimal fix + regression test\n\n---\n\n## Non-negotiable rules\n\n- **No fix without a reproduction** (a failing test, a minimal repro program, or a deterministic HTTP/CLI script).\n- **No durability regressions**: do not weaken WAL/manifest/atomic rename/fsync ordering.\n- **No “drive-by refactors”** while bug hunting; keep patches tight and reviewable.\n- After changes, you must run the full quality suite from `code-quality`.\n\n---\n\n## Discovery phase (required)\n\n### 0) Establish the boundaries\n\nBefore opening files, answer (in notes) these questions:\n\n- Which surface is affected? **CLI**, **HTTP**, **embedded API**, **wasm**, or **ffi**?\n- Is it a **correctness** issue (wrong results), **durability** issue (lost/duplicated data), or **stability** issue (panic/hang)?\n- Does it require a specific feature flag (`vectors`, `zstd`, `gpu`, wasm/IndexedDB, ffi)?\n- Is the failure deterministic or intermittent?\n\n### 1) Baseline the repo (don’t trust your local state)\n\nRun in workspace root:\n\n- `cargo fmt --all`\n- `cargo clippy --all --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo test --all --all-features`\n\nIf anything fails here, you may be chasing a known failure; fix/resolve that first.\n\n### 2) Map the architecture you’re about to debug\n\nCreate a quick map in notes (1–2 minutes):\n\n- `searchlite-core`: schema, indexing, WAL/manifest, segments, query execution, filters/aggs, vectors\n- `searchlite-cli`: user-facing commands and JSON output formatting\n- `searchlite-http`: endpoints (/init, /add, /bulk, /delete, /commit, /refresh, /search, /inspect, /stats, /compact), limits/timeouts/concurrency\n- `searchlite-wasm`: bindings + IndexedDB storage semantics (no fsync)\n- `searchlite-ffi`: C ABI / safety edges\n\nThis map guides where you look first.\n\n### 3) Reproduce the bug with the smallest possible corpus\n\nProduce a “minimal reproducible case” artifact set:\n\n- a schema JSON (small)\n- a small NDJSON/doc list (5–50 docs)\n- one request (HTTP JSON or CLI command) that fails\n\nFor HTTP:\n\n- include the server flags/env (bind addr, index path, max-body-bytes, max-concurrency, request-timeout, refresh-on-commit)\n\nFor CLI:\n\n- include exact commands and any flags\n\n**Goal:** a script a teammate can run in <60 seconds.\n\n### 4) Turn on observability (don’t add prints yet)\n\nUse existing debugging features first:\n\n- For search correctness: add `explain: true` to the request.\n- For performance/odd slowdowns while reproducing: add `profile: true`.\n- For server behavior: run with `RUST_LOG=debug` (or more targeted module filters) and capture the relevant lines.\n\nIf your issue is “writes not visible,” verify lifecycle:\n\n- you must `commit`\n- you may need `/refresh` in HTTP depending on config\n\n### 5) Narrow the fault line by bisecting the pipeline\n\nPick one axis at a time:\n\n**Correctness axis**\n\n- Does the doc get ingested successfully?\n- Does it appear in `/stats` documents?\n- Does `/inspect` show a new segment after commit?\n- Does the query match in bm25 mode vs wand/bmw mode?\n\n**Durability axis**\n\n- Is WAL appended correctly?\n- Is manifest updated atomically?\n- Is WAL truncated only after manifest persistence?\n- After restart, does replay do the expected thing?\n\n**HTTP axis**\n\n- Is the request being rejected due to max body / timeouts / concurrency?\n- Is NDJSON streaming partial and rolling back?\n- Are errors correctly surfaced as `{\"error\":{\"type\",\"reason\"}}`?\n\n### 6) Perform a targeted static sweep of the suspected modules\n\nOnce you know the rough area, do a deliberate scan for bug smells:\n\nSearch patterns to grep/ripgrep for in the relevant crate:\n\n- panics: `unwrap()`, `expect(`, `panic!`, `unreachable!`, `todo!`\n- suspicious error handling: `map_err(|_|`, `ok()?` in non-optional contexts, silent `let _ =`\n- integer edge cases: casts (`as usize`), underflow (`- 1`), unchecked indexing\n- concurrency hazards: `Mutex`/`RwLock` lock ordering, `.await` while holding locks, channels without bounds\n- IO hazards: missing `fsync`, non-atomic file replace, partial writes not handled, directory fsync omissions\n- schema mismatch hazards: stringly-typed field lookups, analyzer lookup defaults, missing nested path validation\n- vector hazards: dimension mismatch, normalization assumptions, unchecked candidate sizing, `NaN` propagation\n\nYou are not “fixing” in this step—just identifying suspects.\n\n### 7) Dynamic bug probes by subsystem (choose what fits)\n\n#### A) WAL / manifest / commit / rollback\n\nIf you suspect commit/durability issues:\n\n- Reproduce a crash-window scenario:\n  1. ingest docs\n  2. start commit\n  3. force termination mid-way (or simulate via test hooks if present)\n  4. restart and observe replay\n- Validate the invariants:\n  - manifest atomic update (rename) and directory sync\n  - WAL truncation happens after manifest sync\n  - rollback cleans new segment artifacts\n\nIf you can’t safely crash in tests, create a unit test around writer/commit phases and validate state.\n\n#### B) Segment lifecycle / compaction / cleanup\n\nIf you see duplicates, ghosts, or bloat:\n\n- Inspect segments via `inspect` and compare to `stats`\n- Run compaction and verify:\n  - live docs preserved\n  - deleted/tombstoned dropped\n  - old segment files removed (or expected to remain until cleanup)\n\n#### C) Query execution modes\n\nIf you suspect scoring/pruning bugs:\n\n- Run the same query with `execution=bm25`, `execution=wand`, `execution=bmw`\n- Results should match for deterministic corpora (unless the contract explicitly says otherwise)\n- If they diverge, you likely have a pruning-bound bug or block-max metadata mismatch\n\n#### D) Filters/aggs/nested correctness\n\nIf filters/aggs are wrong:\n\n- Verify required fields are `fast: true`\n- For nested, verify the filter uses a `Nested` block and that clauses bind to the same object instance\n- Add a repro doc with two nested objects that would catch “cross-object” leakage\n\n#### E) Vectors (feature `vectors`)\n\nIf vector behavior is wrong:\n\n- Check dimension mismatch handling\n- Check cosine normalization expectations\n- Confirm ANN parameters (`candidate_size`, `ef_search`) don’t overflow or accept nonsensical values\n- Verify hybrid search doesn’t double-count or drop vector scores\n\n---\n\n## Fix phase (required)\n\n### 1) Write the failing regression test first\n\n- Prefer a unit test in the most local crate if possible.\n- If the bug is surface-level behavior (HTTP contract, CLI output), add an integration test.\n- Make it deterministic and small.\n- Assert on structure, not strings (parse JSON output).\n\n### 2) Implement the minimal fix\n\n- Tight patch, minimal diff.\n- Keep durability semantics intact.\n- Avoid introducing allocations/locks in hot paths unless justified.\n\n### 3) Prove it\n\nRun:\n\n- `cargo test --all --all-features`\n- Any relevant examples (e.g. pruning example if you touched pruning logic)\n- If the bug touched performance-sensitive code, run the relevant bench before/after.\n\n### 4) Add a “root cause” note\n\nIn the PR description or internal notes, include:\n\n- symptom\n- root cause\n- why the fix is correct\n- what test prevents regressions\n\n---\n\n## Output format (what Codex should produce)\n\nWhen using this skill, produce:\n\n1. **Repro artifact** (schema + docs + request/command)\n2. **Fault localization** (files + functions involved)\n3. **Root cause analysis**\n4. **Fix plan** (minimal changes)\n5. **Regression test** (where it lives and what it asserts)\n6. **Validation commands run** (from code-quality)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T02:51:32.147Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing systematic bug reproduction and resolution capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要系统化错误重现和解决能力的调试Agent。","ja":"体系的なバグの再現と解決機能を必要とするデバッグAgentに最適です。","ko":"체계적인 버그 재현 및 해결 기능이 필요한 디버깅 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de depuración que necesitan capacidades de reproducción y resolución de errores sistemáticos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de débogage nécessitant des capacités de reproduction et de résolution de bogues systématiques.","de":"Perfekt für Debugging-Agents, die systematische Fehlernachstellung und -behebungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Depuração que necessitam de capacidades sistemáticas de reprodução e resolução de bugs.","ru":"Идеально подходит для отладочных агентов, которым требуются систематические возможности воспроизведения и устранения ошибок.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التصحيح التي تحتاج إلى قدرات منهجية لإعادة إنتاج الأخطاء وحلها."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically discover and fix implementation bugs using techniques like BM25 with phrase matching, while ensuring correctness and durability through minimal fixes and regression tests, all via a clean Rust API and optional C/WASM bindings.","zh":"通过诸如BM25与短语匹配等技术，赋能Agent系统地发现并修复实现中的错误，同时通过最小化修复和回归测试确保正确性和持久性，所有功能均通过简洁的Rust API和可选的C/WASM绑定提供。","ja":"BM25とフレーズマッチングなどの技術を使用して、Agentが実装上のバグを体系的に発見し修正できるようにし、最小限の修正と回帰テストを通じて正確性と耐久性を確保します。すべてはクリーンなRust APIとオプションのC/WASMバインディングを介して提供されます。","ko":"BM25와 구문 매칭과 같은 기술을 사용하여 에이전트가 구현 버그를 체계적으로 발견하고 수정할 수 있도록 하며, 최소한의 수정과 회귀 테스트를 통해 정확성과 내구성을 보장합니다. 모든 기능은 깔끔한 Rust API와 선택적인 C/WASM 바인딩을 통해 제공됩니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a descubrir y solucionar errores de implementación de forma sistemática utilizando técnicas como BM25 con coincidencia de frases, garantizando la corrección y durabilidad a través de soluciones mínimas y pruebas de regresión, todo a través de una API de Rust limpia y enlaces opcionales C/WASM.","fr":"Permet aux agents de découvrir et de corriger systématiquement les bogues d''implémentation en utilisant des techniques comme BM25 avec correspondance de phrases, en garantissant la correction et la durabilité grâce à des corrections minimales et des tests de régression, le tout via une API Rust propre et des liaisons C/WASM optionnelles.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Implementierungsfehler systematisch zu entdecken und zu beheben, indem Techniken wie BM25 mit Phrasenübereinstimmung verwendet werden, während Korrektheit und Haltbarkeit durch minimale Korrekturen und Regressionsprüfungen sichergestellt werden, alles über eine saubere Rust-API und optionale C/WASM-Bindungen.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a descobrir e corrigir bugs de implementação de forma sistemática usando técnicas como BM25 com correspondência de frases, garantindo a correção e a durabilidade por meio de correções mínimas e testes de regressão, tudo por meio de uma API Rust limpa e vinculações opcionais C/WASM.","ru":"Позволяет агентам систематически обнаруживать и исправлять ошибки реализации с использованием таких методов, как BM25 с сопоставлением фраз, обеспечивая корректность и надежность за счет минимальных исправлений и регрессионных тестов, все через чистый Rust API и опциональные привязки C/WASM.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من اكتشاف وإصلاح أخطاء التنفيذ بشكل منهجي باستخدام تقنيات مثل BM25 مع مطابقة العبارات، مع ضمان الصحة والمتانة من خلال إصلاحات بسيطة واختبارات ارتدادية، كل ذلك عبر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Rust نظيفة وروابط اختيارية لـ C/WASM."},"useCases":{"en":["Reproducing elusive bugs with deterministic HTTP/CLI scripts","Narrowing bug scope using filters and aggregations","Creating minimal repro programs for efficient debugging"],"zh":["使用确定性的HTTP/CLI脚本来重现难以捉摸的错误","使用过滤器和聚合功能缩小错误范围","创建最小化的重现程序以进行高效调试"],"ja":["決定論的HTTP/CLIスクリプトを使用した捉えにくいバグの再現","フィルターと集計を使用したバグ範囲の絞り込み","効率的なデバッグのための最小限の再現プログラムの作成"],"ko":["결정론적인 HTTP/CLI 스크립트로 파악하기 어려운 버그 재현","필터와 집계를 사용하여 버그 범위 축소","효율적인 디버깅을 위한 최소 재현 프로그램 생성"],"es":["Reproducir errores esquivos con scripts HTTP/CLI deterministas","Reducir el alcance de los errores utilizando filtros y agregaciones","Crear programas de reproducción mínimos para una depuración eficiente"],"fr":["Reproduire des bogues insaisissables avec des scripts HTTP/CLI déterministes","Réduire la portée des bogues en utilisant des filtres et des agrégations","Créer des programmes de reproduction minimaux pour un débogage efficace"],"de":["Schwierige Fehler mit deterministischen HTTP/CLI-Skripten reproduzieren","Fehlerumfang mit Filtern und Aggregationen einschränken","Erstellen von minimalen Reproduktionsprogrammen für effizientes Debugging"],"pt":["Reproduzir bugs elusivos com scripts HTTP/CLI determinísticos","Reduzir o escopo do bug usando filtros e agregações","Criar programas de reprodução mínima para depuração eficiente"],"ru":["Воспроизведение неуловимых ошибок с помощью детерминированных HTTP/CLI скриптов","Сужение области ошибки с использованием фильтров и агрегаций","Создание минимальных программ воспроизведения для эффективной отладки"],"ar":["إعادة إنتاج الأخطاء بعيدة المنال باستخدام نصوص HTTP/CLI حتمية","تضييق نطاق الخطأ باستخدام المرشحات والتجميعات","إنشاء برامج إعادة إنتاج بسيطة لتصحيح فعال"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires a failing test or minimal repro program for bug fixing","No fix allowed without a clear reproduction","Must ensure no durability regressions"],"zh":["需要失败的测试或最小化的重现程序来进行错误修复","没有明确的复现步骤则不允许进行修复","必须确保不会产生持久性回归"],"ja":["バグ修正には失敗したテストまたは最小限の再現プログラムが必要","明確な再現手順なしでは修正が許可されない","耐久性の回帰がないことを確認する必要がある"],"ko":["버그 수정을 위해 실패한 테스트 또는 최소 재현 프로그램이 필요함","명확한 재현 없이는 수정이 허용되지 않음","내구성 회귀가 없음을 반드시 확인해야 함"],"es":["Requiere una prueba fallida o un programa de reproducción mínimo para la corrección de errores","No se permite la corrección sin una reproducción clara","Deben asegurarse de que no haya regresiones de durabilidad"],"fr":["Nécessite un test qui échoue ou un programme de reproduction minimal pour la correction des bogues","Aucune correction n''est autorisée sans une reproduction claire","Il faut s''assurer qu''il n''y a pas de régression de durabilité"],"de":["Benötigt einen fehlgeschlagenen Test oder ein minimales Reproduktionsprogramm zur Fehlernbehebung","Keine Korrektur ohne klare Reproduktion erlaubt","Es muss sichergestellt werden, dass es keine Haltbarkeitsrückschritte gibt"],"pt":["Requer um teste com falha ou um programa mínimo de reprodução para corrigir o bug","Nenhuma correção permitida sem uma reprodução clara","Deve garantir que não haja regressões de durabilidade"],"ru":["Требует проваленного теста или минимальной программы воспроизведения для исправления ошибки","Исправление не допускается без четкого воспроизведения","Необходимо гарантировать отсутствие регрессий надежности"],"ar":["يتطلب اختبارًا فاشلًا أو برنامج إعادة إنتاج بسيط لإصلاح الخطأ","لا يسمح بالإصلاح دون إعادة إنتاج واضحة","يجب التأكد من عدم وجود تراجعات في المتانة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"660c80c3b1fd791f588f35f79368ec5d2096b44b8b23f77c53a0392ea06b7d36","qualityScore":50}');
