React и Node.js","Анализ SEO с помощью Python и CLI","Улучшение рейтинга сайтов","Инструменты аудита SEO","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами","Поддержка разработчиков"],"ar":["تحسين مواقع الويب باستخدام React و Node.js","تحليل إدارة محركات البحث باستخدام Python و CLI","تحسين تصنيف المواقع","أدوات تدقيق إدارة محركات البحث","التكامل مع أدوات إدارة محركات البحث","دعم المطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["程序化SEO","AI智能工具","SEO优化","开发效率","网站性能","React","Node.js","CLI工具"],"ja":["プログラムSEO","AIエージェント","SEO最適化","開発効率","ウェブサイトパフォーマンス","React","Node.js","CLIツール"],"ko":["프로그래밍 SEO","AI 에이전트","SEO 최적화","개발 효율성","웹사이트 성능","React","Node.js","CLI 도구"],"es":["cómo usar herramientas de SEO programático","qué es el SEO programático","alternativas a herramientas de SEO","SEO programático vs SEO tradicional","instalación de herramientas de SEO","guía de configuración de SEO programático","herramientas de SEO para desarrolladores","mejores prácticas de SEO programático"],"fr":["comment utiliser des outils de SEO programmé","qu''est-ce que le SEO programmé","alternatives aux outils de SEO","SEO programmé vs SEO traditionnel","installation d''outils de SEO","guide de configuration de SEO programmé","outils de SEO pour les développeurs","meilleures pratiques de SEO programmé"],"de":["wie man programmatische SEO-Tools verwendet","was ist der programmatische SEO","Alternativen zu SEO-Tools","programmatischer SEO vs traditioneller SEO","Installation von SEO-Tools","Konfigurationsanleitung für programmatischen SEO","SEO-Tools für Entwickler","beste Praktiken für programmatischen SEO"],"pt":["como usar SEO programático","o que é SEO programático","ferramentas de SEO para desenvolvedores","SEO programático vs SEO tradicional","instalar SEO programático","guia de configuração de SEO programático","melhorias de SEO para sites","otimização de sites com Python","análise de SEO com React"],"ru":["как использовать программное SEO","что такое программное SEO","инструменты SEO для разработчиков","программное SEO vs традиционное SEO","установить программное SEO","руководство по настройке программного SEO","улучшения SEO для сайтов","оптимизация сайтов с помощью Python","анализ SEO с помощью React"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام إدارة محركات البحث البرمجية","ما هي إدارة محركات البحث البرمجية","أدوات إدارة محركات البحث لمانحين","إدارة محركات البحث البرمجية vs إدارة محركات البحث التقليدية","تثبيت إدارة محركات البحث البرمجية","دليل إعداد إدارة محركات البحث البرمجية","تحسينات إدارة محركات البحث للمواقع","تحسين مواقع الويب باستخدام Python","تحليل إدارة محركات البحث باستخدام React"]}},"owner":"dipenmagdani","repo":"portfolio-v2","repoPath":"dipenmagdani/portfolio-v2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T11:09:17Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"programmatic-seo","description":"When the user wants to create SEO-driven pages at scale using templates and data. Also use when the user mentions programmatic SEO, template pages, pages at scale, directory pages, location pages, [keyword] + [city] pages, comparison pages, integration pages, or building many pages for SEO. For auditing existing SEO issues, see seo-audit.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Programmatic SEO\n\nYou are an expert in programmatic SEO—building SEO-optimized pages at scale using templates and data. Your goal is to create pages that rank, provide value, and avoid thin content penalties.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore designing a programmatic SEO strate","body":"# Programmatic SEO\n\nYou are an expert in programmatic SEO—building SEO-optimized pages at scale using templates and data. Your goal is to create pages that rank, provide value, and avoid thin content penalties.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore designing a programmatic SEO strategy, understand:\n\n1. **Business Context**\n   - What''s the product/service?\n   - Who is the target audience?\n   - What''s the conversion goal for these pages?\n\n2. **Opportunity Assessment**\n   - What search patterns exist?\n   - How many potential pages?\n   - What''s the search volume distribution?\n\n3. **Competitive Landscape**\n   - Who ranks for these terms now?\n   - What do their pages look like?\n   - Can you realistically compete?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Unique Value Per Page\n- Every page must provide value specific to that page\n- Not just swapped variables in a template\n- Maximize unique content—the more differentiated, the better\n\n### 2. Proprietary Data Wins\nHierarchy of data defensibility:\n1. Proprietary (you created it)\n2. Product-derived (from your users)\n3. User-generated (your community)\n4. Licensed (exclusive access)\n5. Public (anyone can use—weakest)\n\n### 3. Clean URL Structure\n**Always use subfolders, not subdomains**:\n- Good: `yoursite.com/templates/resume/`\n- Bad: `templates.yoursite.com/resume/`\n\n### 4. Genuine Search Intent Match\nPages must actually answer what people are searching for.\n\n### 5. Quality Over Quantity\nBetter to have 100 great pages than 10,000 thin ones.\n\n### 6. Avoid Google Penalties\n- No doorway pages\n- No keyword stuffing\n- No duplicate content\n- Genuine utility for users\n\n---\n\n## The 12 Playbooks (Overview)\n\n| Playbook | Pattern | Example |\n|----------|---------|---------|\n| Templates | \"[Type] template\" | \"resume template\" |\n| Curation | \"best [category]\" | \"best website builders\" |\n| Conversions | \"[X] to [Y]\" | \"$10 USD to GBP\" |\n| Comparisons | \"[X] vs [Y]\" | \"webflow vs wordpress\" |\n| Examples | \"[type] examples\" | \"landing page examples\" |\n| Locations | \"[service] in [location]\" | \"dentists in austin\" |\n| Personas | \"[product] for [audience]\" | \"crm for real estate\" |\n| Integrations | \"[product A] [product B] integration\" | \"slack asana integration\" |\n| Glossary | \"what is [term]\" | \"what is pSEO\" |\n| Translations | Content in multiple languages | Localized content |\n| Directory | \"[category] tools\" | \"ai copywriting tools\" |\n| Profiles | \"[entity name]\" | \"stripe ceo\" |\n\n**For detailed playbook implementation**: See [references/playbooks.md](references/playbooks.md)\n\n---\n\n## Choosing Your Playbook\n\n| If you have... | Consider... |\n|----------------|-------------|\n| Proprietary data | Directories, Profiles |\n| Product with integrations | Integrations |\n| Design/creative product | Templates, Examples |\n| Multi-segment audience | Personas |\n| Local presence | Locations |\n| Tool or utility product | Conversions |\n| Content/expertise | Glossary, Curation |\n| Competitor landscape | Comparisons |\n\nYou can layer multiple playbooks (e.g., \"Best coworking spaces in San Diego\").\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Framework\n\n### 1. Keyword Pattern Research\n\n**Identify the pattern:**\n- What''s the repeating structure?\n- What are the variables?\n- How many unique combinations exist?\n\n**Validate demand:**\n- Aggregate search volume\n- Volume distribution (head vs. long tail)\n- Trend direction\n\n### 2. Data Requirements\n\n**Identify data sources:**\n- What data populates each page?\n- Is it first-party, scraped, licensed, public?\n- How is it updated?\n\n### 3. Template Design\n\n**Page structure:**\n- Header with target keyword\n- Unique intro (not just variables swapped)\n- Data-driven sections\n- Related pages / internal links\n- CTAs appropriate to intent\n\n**Ensuring uniqueness:**\n- Each page needs unique value\n- Conditional content based on data\n- Original insights/analysis per page\n\n### 4. Internal Linking Architecture\n\n**Hub and spoke model:**\n- Hub: Main category page\n- Spokes: Individual programmatic pages\n- Cross-links between related spokes\n\n**Avoid orphan pages:**\n- Every page reachable from main site\n- XML sitemap for all pages\n- Breadcrumbs with structured data\n\n### 5. Indexation Strategy\n\n- Prioritize high-volume patterns\n- Noindex very thin variations\n- Manage crawl budget thoughtfully\n- Separate sitemaps by page type\n\n---\n\n## Quality Checks\n\n### Pre-Launch Checklist\n\n**Content quality:**\n- [ ] Each page provides unique value\n- [ ] Answers search intent\n- [ ] Readable and useful\n\n**Technical SEO:**\n- [ ] Unique titles and meta descriptions\n- [ ] Proper heading structure\n- [ ] Schema markup implemented\n- [ ] Page speed acceptable\n\n**Internal linking:**\n- [ ] Connected to site architecture\n- [ ] Related pages linked\n- [ ] No orphan pages\n\n**Indexation:**\n- [ ] In XML sitemap\n- [ ] Crawlable\n- [ ] No conflicting noindex\n\n### Post-Launch Monitoring\n\nTrack: Indexation rate, Rankings, Traffic, Engagement, Conversion\n\nWatch for: Thin content warnings, Ranking drops, Manual actions, Crawl errors\n\n---\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n- **Thin content**: Just swapping city names in identical content\n- **Keyword cannibalization**: Multiple pages targeting same keyword\n- **Over-generation**: Creating pages with no search demand\n- **Poor data quality**: Outdated or incorrect information\n- **Ignoring UX**: Pages exist for Google, not users\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Strategy Document\n- Opportunity analysis\n- Implementation plan\n- Content guidelines\n\n### Page Template\n- URL structure\n- Title/meta templates\n- Content outline\n- Schema markup\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What keyword patterns are you targeting?\n2. What data do you have (or can acquire)?\n3. How many pages are you planning?\n4. What does your site authority look like?\n5. Who currently ranks for these terms?\n6. What''s your technical stack?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **seo-audit**: For auditing programmatic pages after launch\n- **schema-markup**: For adding structured data\n- **competitor-alternatives**: For comparison page frameworks\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T07:13:15.895Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing scalable SEO optimization through template-based page generation and data-driven content creation.","zh":"非常适合需要通过模板基于页面生成和数据驱动内容创建实现可扩展SEO优化的AI代理。","ja":"テンプレートベースのページ生成とデータドリブンのコンテンツ作成を通じて拡張可能なSEO最適化が必要なAIエージェントに最適。","ko":"템플릿 기반 페이지 생성 및 데이터 驱动 콘텐츠 생성을 통해 확장 가능한 SEO 최적화를 필요로 하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan una optimización de SEO escalable a través de la generación de páginas basadas en plantillas y la creación de contenido impulsada por datos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui ont besoin d''une optimisation de SEO scalable via la génération de pages basée sur des modèles et la création de contenu pilotée par des données.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die eine skalierbare SEO-Optimierung durch templatebasierte Seiten generierung und datengetriebene Inhalts erstellung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de otimização de SEO escalável por meio de geração de páginas baseada em templates e criação de conteúdo orientada a dados.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым необходима масштабируемая оптимизация SEO посредством генерации страниц на основе шаблонов и создания контента, управляемого данными.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي التي تحتاج إلى تحسين محركات البحث القابل للتحجيم من خلال إنشاء صفحات قائم على القوالب وإنشاء المحتوى القائم على البيانات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build SEO-optimized pages at scale using templates and data, avoiding thin content penalties and providing value to users through structured data and comprehensive content analysis, leveraging protocols like HTML and file formats like .md.","zh":"赋予代理构建大规模SEO优化页面的能力，使用模板和数据，避免薄内容惩罚，并通过结构化数据和综合内容分析为用户提供价值，利用HTML等协议和.md等文件格式。","ja":"エージェントがテンプレートとデータを使用して大規模にSEO最適化されたページを構築する能力を付与し、薄いコンテンツのペナルティを回避し、HTMLなどのプロトコルや.mdなどのファイル形式を利用して構造化されたデータと包括的なコンテンツ分析を通じてユーザーに価値を提供する。","ko":"에이전트가 템플릿과 데이터를 사용하여 대규모로 SEO 최적화된 페이지를 구축할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 얇은 콘텐츠의 페널티를 피하고, HTML 등의 프로토콜과 .md 등의 파일 형식을 활용하여 구조화된 데이터와 포괄적인 콘텐츠 분석을 통해 사용자에게 가치를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear páginas optimizadas para SEO a gran escala utilizando plantillas y datos, evitando las penalizaciones por contenido delgado y brindando valor a los usuarios a través de datos estructurados y un análisis de contenido integral, aprovechando protocolos como HTML y formatos de archivo como .md.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des pages optimisées pour le SEO à grande échelle en utilisant des modèles et des données, en évitant les pénalités pour contenu mince et en fournissant de la valeur aux utilisateurs grâce à des données structurées et à une analyse de contenu complète, en exploitant des protocoles comme HTML et des formats de fichiers comme .md.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, SEO-optimierte Seiten im großen Maßstab zu erstellen, indem sie Vorlagen und Daten verwenden, Thin-Content-Strafen vermeiden und den Benutzern durch strukturierte Daten und eine umfassende Inhaltsanalyse Wert bieten, indem sie Protokolle wie HTML und Dateiformate wie .md nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir páginas otimizadas para SEO em larga escala, utilizando templates e dados, evitando penalidades de conteúdo fino e fornecendo valor aos usuários por meio de dados estruturados e análise abrangente de conteúdo, aproveitando protocolos como HTML e formatos de arquivo como .md.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать страницы, оптимизированные для SEO, в крупном масштабе, используя шаблоны и данные, избегая штрафов за тонкий контент и предоставляя пользователям ценность посредством структурированных данных и комплексного анализа контента, используя протоколы, такие как HTML, и форматы файлов, такие как .md.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من إنشاء صفحات محسنة لتحسين محركات البحث على نطاق واسع باستخدام القوالب والبيانات، وتجنب جزاءات المحتوى الرفيع، وتقديم قيمة للمستخدمين من خلال البيانات المنظمة والتحليل الشامل للمحتوى، واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل HTML وتنسيقات الملفات مثل .md."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating SEO page generation","Generating data-driven content for product marketing","Optimizing page templates for search engine ranking"],"zh":["自动化SEO页面生成","为产品营销生成数据驱动内容","优化页面模板以提高搜索引擎排名"],"ja":["SEOページ生成の自動化","製品マーケティングのためのデータドリブンのコンテンツ生成","検索エンジンランキングの向上のためのページテンプレートの最適化"],"ko":["SEO 페이지 생성 자동화","제품 마케팅을 위한 데이터 驱动 콘텐츠 생성","검색 엔진 순위 향상을 위한 페이지 템플릿 최적화"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de páginas de SEO","Generación de contenido impulsado por datos para marketing de productos","Optimización de plantillas de páginas para el ranking de motores de búsqueda"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de pages de SEO","Génération de contenu piloté par des données pour le marketing de produits","Optimisation de modèles de pages pour le référencement de moteurs de recherche"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von SEO-Seiten","Erstellung von datengetriebenem Inhalt für Produktmarketing","Optimierung von Seitenvorlagen für die Suchmaschinenrangliste"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de páginas de SEO","Gerar conteúdo orientado a dados para marketing de produtos","Otimizar modelos de páginas para classificação de mecanismos de busca"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию страниц SEO","Генерировать контент, управляемый данными, для маркетинга продуктов","Оптимизировать шаблоны страниц для рейтинга поисковых систем"],"ar":["تحسين تلقائي لإنشاء صفحات تحسين محركات البحث","إنشاء محتوى قائم على البيانات للتسويق بالمنتجات","تحسين قوالب الصفحات لترتيب محركات البحث"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires product marketing context","Needs access to .claude/product-marketing-context.md file"],"zh":["需要产品营销背景","需要访问.claude/product-marketing-context.md文件"],"ja":["製品マーケティングのコンテキストが必要",".claude/product-marketing-context.mdファイルへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["제품 마케팅 배경이 필요",".claude/product-marketing-context.md 파일에 액세스해야 함"],"es":["Requiere contexto de marketing de productos","Necesita acceso al archivo .claude/product-marketing-context.md"],"fr":["Nécessite un contexte de marketing de produits","A besoin d''un accès au fichier .claude/product-marketing-context.md"],"de":["Benötigt Produktmarketing-Kontext","Benötigt Zugriff auf die Datei .claude/product-marketing-context.md"],"pt":["Exige contexto de marketing de produtos","Necessita acesso ao arquivo .claude/product-marketing-context.md"],"ru":["Требует контекста маркетинга продуктов","Требует доступа к файлу .claude/product-marketing-context.md"],"ar":["يتطلب سياق تسويق المنتجات","يتطلب الوصول إلى الملف .claude/product-marketing-context.md"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0602e928f430986fa712a31335c915c4b594f51dfbef122e01304b855d724f75","qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kreuzberg-dev/kreuzberg/kreuzberg', 'community', 'kreuzberg-dev', 'kreuzberg', 'kreuzberg-dev/kreuzberg', 'kreuzberg', 0, 0, 50, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.879Z', '2026-03-02T02:08:07.574Z', '4ec8fa91d9dd48bafcb32556b244d2198f6745dfadfad81fe33d33b8b3f8d316', '{"id":"kreuzberg-dev/kreuzberg/kreuzberg","name":"kreuzberg","description":{"zh":"Kreuzberg 是一个高性能的文档智能库，支持多种编程语言，包括 Rust、Python、Node.js/TypeScript 等","ja":"Kreuzberg は、高性能のドキュメントインテリジェンスライブラリで、Rust、Python、Node.js/TypeScript など複数のプログラミング言語をサポートします","ko":"Kreuzberg는 고성능 문서 인텔리전스 라이브러리로서 Rust, Python, Node.js/TypeScript 등을 포함한 여러 프로그래밍 언어를 지원합니다","es":"Kreuzberg es una biblioteca de inteligencia de documentos de alto rendimiento con núcleo de Rust y enlaces nativos para varios lenguajes","fr":"Kreuzberg est une bibliothèque d''intelligence de documents haute performance avec un noyau Rust et des liens natifs pour plusieurs langages","de":"Kreuzberg ist eine Hochleistungs-Bibliothek für Dokumenten-Intelligenz mit Rust-Kern und nativen Bindings für mehrere Sprachen","pt":"Kreuzberg é uma biblioteca de inteligência de documentos de alto desempenho com núcleo em Rust e vinculações nativas para Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, PHP e Elixir.","ru":"Kreuzberg - это высокопроизводительная библиотека документальной разведки с ядром на Rust и родными привязками для Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, PHP и Elixir.","ar":"Kreuzberg هي مكتبة ذكاء المستندات عالية الأداء مع نواة في Rust وربطات الأصلي ل Python و Node.js/TypeScript و Ruby و Go و Java و C# و PHP و Elixir.","en":"A polyglot document intelligence framework with a Rust core. Extract text, metadata, and structured information from PDFs, Office documents, images, and 75+ formats. Available for Rust, Python, Ruby, Java, Go, PHP, Elixir, C#, TypeScript (Node/Bun/Wasm/Deno)- or use via CLI, REST API, or MCP server."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Kreuzberg 文档提取框架","ja":"Kreuzberg ドキュメント抽出フレームワーク","ko":"Kreuzberg 문서 추출 프레임워크","es":"Kreuzberg: Extracción de Documentos Inteligentes","fr":"Kreuzberg: Extraction de Documents Intelligents","de":"Kreuzberg: Intelligente Dokumentenextraktion","pt":"Kreuzberg: Extração de Documentos em Rust","ru":"Kreuzberg: Фреймворк для извлечения данных из документов","ar":"Kreuzberg: إطار عمل ذكاء المستندات متعدد اللغات","en":"kreuzberg"},"description":{"zh":"Kreuzberg 是一个高性能的文档智能库，支持多种编程语言，包括 Rust、Python、Node.js/TypeScript 等","ja":"Kreuzberg は、高性能のドキュメントインテリジェンスライブラリで、Rust、Python、Node.js/TypeScript など複数のプログラミング言語をサポートします","ko":"Kreuzberg는 고성능 문서 인텔리전스 라이브러리로서 Rust, Python, Node.js/TypeScript 등을 포함한 여러 프로그래밍 언어를 지원합니다","es":"Kreuzberg es una biblioteca de inteligencia de documentos de alto rendimiento con núcleo de Rust y enlaces nativos para varios lenguajes","fr":"Kreuzberg est une bibliothèque d''intelligence de documents haute performance avec un noyau Rust et des liens natifs pour plusieurs langages","de":"Kreuzberg ist eine Hochleistungs-Bibliothek für Dokumenten-Intelligenz mit Rust-Kern und nativen Bindings für mehrere Sprachen","pt":"Kreuzberg é uma biblioteca de inteligência de documentos de alto desempenho com núcleo em Rust e vinculações nativas para Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, G...","ru":"Kreuzberg - это высокопроизводительная библиотека документальной разведки с ядром на Rust и родными привязками для Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java...","ar":"Kreuzberg هي مكتبة ذكاء المستندات عالية الأداء مع نواة في Rust وربطات الأصلي ل Python و Node.js/TypeScript و Ruby و Go و Java و C# و PHP و Elixir.","en":"A polyglot document intelligence framework with a Rust core. Extract text, metadata, and structured information from PDFs, Office documents, images, and 75+ ..."},"definition":{"en":"A polyglot document intelligence framework with a Rust core. Extract text, metadata, and structured information from PDFs, Office documents, images, and 75+ formats. Available for Rust, Python, Ruby, Java, Go, PHP, Elixir, C#, TypeScript (Node/Bun/Wasm/Deno)- or use via CLI, REST API, or MCP server."},"features":{"zh":["支持 75+ 格式的文档提取","高性能的文档智能库","支持多种编程语言","包括 PDF、Office 文档、图像等格式","支持 OCR 功能","提供 CLI、REST API 和 MCP 服务器接口"],"ja":["75 種類以上の形式のドキュメント抽出をサポート","高性能のドキュメントインテリジェンスライブラリ","複数のプログラミング言語をサポート","PDF、Office ドキュメント、画像などをサポート","OCR 機能をサポート","CLI、REST API、MCP サーバーインターフェースを提供"],"ko":["75종 이상의 형식의 문서 추출을 지원","고성능 문서 인텔리전스 라이브러리","여러 프로그래밍 언어를 지원","PDF, Office 문서, 이미지 등을 지원","OCR 기능을 지원","CLI, REST API, MCP 서버 인터페이스를 제공"],"es":["Extracción de texto y metadatos de documentos","Reconocimiento óptico de caracteres (OCR) para documentos escaneados","Soporte para 75+ formatos de archivo","Enlaces nativos para Rust, Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, PHP y Elixir","Interfaz de línea de comandos, API REST y servidor MCP"],"fr":["Extraction de texte et de métadonnées de documents","Reconnaissance optique de caractères (OCR) pour les documents scannés","Prise en charge de 75+ formats de fichiers","Liens natifs pour Rust, Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, PHP et Elixir","Interface de ligne de commande, API REST et serveur MCP"],"de":["Extraktion von Text und Metadaten aus Dokumenten","Optische Zeichenerkennung (OCR) für gescannte Dokumente","Unterstützung für 75+ Dateiformate","Native Bindings für Rust, Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, PHP und Elixir","Kommandozeilen-Interface, REST-API und MCP-Server"],"pt":["Extração de texto e metadados de documentos","Reconhecimento óptico de caracteres (OCR) em imagens e documentos digitalizados","Suporte a 75+ formatos de arquivos","Vinculações nativas para várias linguagens de programação","Alto desempenho e escalabilidade"],"ru":["Извлечение текста и метаданных из документов","Оптическое распознавание символов (OCR) в изображениях и оцифрованных документах","Поддержка 75+ форматов файлов","Родные привязки для нескольких языков программирования","Высокая производительность и масштабируемость"],"ar":["استخراج النص والبيانات الوصفية من المستندات","التعرف البصري على الحروف (OCR) في الصور والوثائق الممسوحة ضوئيًا","دعم 75+ صيغة ملف","ربطات الأصلي لمختلف لغات البرمجة","أداء عالي ومتوافق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["文档智能","文档提取","Kreuzberg","Rust","Python","Node.js/TypeScript","文档分析","OCR","文档处理"],"ja":["ドキュメントインテリジェンス","ドキュメント抽出","Kreuzberg","Rust","Python","Node.js/TypeScript","ドキュメント分析","OCR","ドキュメント処理"],"ko":["문서 인텔리전스","문서 추출","Kreuzberg","Rust","Python","Node.js/TypeScript","문서 분석","OCR","문서 처리"],"es":["inteligencia de documentos","extracción de texto","reconocimiento óptico de caracteres","OCR","formatos de archivo","Rust","Python","Node.js","TypeScript"],"fr":["intelligence de documents","extraction de texte","reconnaissance optique de caractères","OCR","formats de fichiers","Rust","Python","Node.js","TypeScript"],"de":["Dokumenten-Intelligenz","Text-Extraktion","optische Zeichenerkennung","OCR","Dateiformate","Rust","Python","Node.js","TypeScript"],"pt":["Extração de documentos","Inteligência de documentos","Reconhecimento óptico de caracteres","OCR","Biblioteca de documentos","Rust","Python","Node.js","TypeScript"],"ru":["Извлечение документов","Документальная разведка","Оптическое распознавание символов","OCR","Библиотека документов","Rust","Python","Node.js","TypeScript"],"ar":["استخراج المستندات","ذكاء المستندات","التعرف البصري على الحروف","OCR","مكتبة المستندات","Rust","Python","Node.js","TypeScript"]}},"owner":"kreuzberg-dev","repo":"kreuzberg","repoPath":"kreuzberg-dev/kreuzberg","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.879Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kreuzberg","description":">-","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Kreuzberg Document Extraction\n\nKreuzberg is a high-performance document intelligence library with a Rust core and native bindings for Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, PHP, and Elixir. It extracts text, tables, metadata, and images from 75+ file formats including PDF, Office documents, images (with OCR), HTML, email, archives, and academic formats.\n\nUse this skill when writing code that:\n- Extracts text or metadata from documents\n- Performs OCR on scanned documents or images\n- Ba","body":"# Kreuzberg Document Extraction\n\nKreuzberg is a high-performance document intelligence library with a Rust core and native bindings for Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, PHP, and Elixir. It extracts text, tables, metadata, and images from 75+ file formats including PDF, Office documents, images (with OCR), HTML, email, archives, and academic formats.\n\nUse this skill when writing code that:\n- Extracts text or metadata from documents\n- Performs OCR on scanned documents or images\n- Batch-processes multiple files\n- Configures extraction options (output format, chunking, OCR, language detection)\n- Implements custom plugins (post-processors, validators, OCR backends)\n\n## Installation\n\n### Python\n```bash\npip install kreuzberg\n# Optional OCR backends:\npip install kreuzberg[easyocr]    # EasyOCR\npip install kreuzberg[paddleocr]  # PaddleOCR\n```\n\n### Node.js\n```bash\nnpm install @kreuzberg/node\n```\n\n### Rust\n```toml\n# Cargo.toml\n[dependencies]\nkreuzberg = { version = \"4\", features = [\"tokio-runtime\"] }\n# features: tokio-runtime (required for sync + batch), pdf, ocr, chunking,\n#           embeddings, language-detection, keywords-yake, keywords-rake\n```\n\n### CLI\n```bash\n# Download from GitHub releases, or:\ncargo install kreuzberg-cli\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Python (Async)\n```python\nfrom kreuzberg import extract_file\n\nresult = await extract_file(\"document.pdf\")\nprint(result.content)       # extracted text\nprint(result.metadata)      # document metadata\nprint(result.tables)        # extracted tables\n```\n\n### Python (Sync)\n```python\nfrom kreuzberg import extract_file_sync\n\nresult = extract_file_sync(\"document.pdf\")\nprint(result.content)\n```\n\n### Node.js\n```typescript\nimport { extractFile } from ''@kreuzberg/node'';\n\nconst result = await extractFile(''document.pdf'');\nconsole.log(result.content);\nconsole.log(result.metadata);\nconsole.log(result.tables);\n```\n\n### Node.js (Sync)\n```typescript\nimport { extractFileSync } from ''@kreuzberg/node'';\n\nconst result = extractFileSync(''document.pdf'');\n```\n\n### Rust (Async)\n```rust\nuse kreuzberg::{extract_file, ExtractionConfig};\n\n#[tokio::main]\nasync fn main() -> kreuzberg::Result<()> {\n    let config = ExtractionConfig::default();\n    let result = extract_file(\"document.pdf\", None, &config).await?;\n    println!(\"{}\", result.content);\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### Rust (Sync) — requires `tokio-runtime` feature\n```rust\nuse kreuzberg::{extract_file_sync, ExtractionConfig};\n\nfn main() -> kreuzberg::Result<()> {\n    let config = ExtractionConfig::default();\n    let result = extract_file_sync(\"document.pdf\", None, &config)?;\n    println!(\"{}\", result.content);\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### CLI\n```bash\nkreuzberg extract document.pdf\nkreuzberg extract document.pdf --format json\nkreuzberg extract document.pdf --output-format markdown\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nAll languages use the same configuration structure with language-appropriate naming conventions.\n\n### Python (snake_case)\n```python\nfrom kreuzberg import (\n    ExtractionConfig, OcrConfig, TesseractConfig,\n    PdfConfig, ChunkingConfig,\n)\n\nconfig = ExtractionConfig(\n    ocr=OcrConfig(\n        backend=\"tesseract\",\n        language=\"eng\",\n        tesseract_config=TesseractConfig(psm=6, enable_table_detection=True),\n    ),\n    pdf_options=PdfConfig(passwords=[\"secret123\"]),\n    chunking=ChunkingConfig(max_chars=1000, max_overlap=200),\n    output_format=\"markdown\",\n)\n\nresult = await extract_file(\"document.pdf\", config=config)\n```\n\n### Node.js (camelCase)\n```typescript\nimport { extractFile, type ExtractionConfig } from ''@kreuzberg/node'';\n\nconst config: ExtractionConfig = {\n    ocr: { backend: ''tesseract'', language: ''eng'' },\n    pdfOptions: { passwords: [''secret123''] },\n    chunking: { maxChars: 1000, maxOverlap: 200 },\n    outputFormat: ''markdown'',\n};\n\nconst result = await extractFile(''document.pdf'', null, config);\n```\n\n### Rust (snake_case)\n```rust\nuse kreuzberg::{ExtractionConfig, OcrConfig, ChunkingConfig, OutputFormat};\n\nlet config = ExtractionConfig {\n    ocr: Some(OcrConfig {\n        backend: \"tesseract\".into(),\n        language: \"eng\".into(),\n        ..Default::default()\n    }),\n    chunking: Some(ChunkingConfig {\n        max_characters: 1000,\n        overlap: 200,\n        ..Default::default()\n    }),\n    output_format: OutputFormat::Markdown,\n    ..Default::default()\n};\n\nlet result = extract_file(\"document.pdf\", None, &config).await?;\n```\n\n### Config File (TOML)\n```toml\noutput_format = \"markdown\"\n\n[ocr]\nbackend = \"tesseract\"\nlanguage = \"eng\"\n\n[chunking]\nmax_chars = 1000\nmax_overlap = 200\n\n[pdf_options]\npasswords = [\"secret123\"]\n```\n\n```bash\n# CLI: auto-discovers kreuzberg.toml in current/parent directories\nkreuzberg extract doc.pdf\n# or explicit:\nkreuzberg extract doc.pdf --config kreuzberg.toml\nkreuzberg extract doc.pdf --config-json ''{\"ocr\":{\"backend\":\"tesseract\",\"language\":\"deu\"}}''\n```\n\n## Batch Processing\n\n### Python\n```python\nfrom kreuzberg import batch_extract_files, batch_extract_files_sync\n\n# Async\nresults = await batch_extract_files([\"doc1.pdf\", \"doc2.docx\", \"doc3.xlsx\"])\n\n# Sync\nresults = batch_extract_files_sync([\"doc1.pdf\", \"doc2.docx\"])\n\nfor result in results:\n    print(f\"{len(result.content)} chars extracted\")\n```\n\n### Node.js\n```typescript\nimport { batchExtractFiles } from ''@kreuzberg/node'';\n\nconst results = await batchExtractFiles([''doc1.pdf'', ''doc2.docx'']);\n```\n\n### Rust — requires `tokio-runtime` feature\n```rust\nuse kreuzberg::{batch_extract_file, ExtractionConfig};\n\nlet config = ExtractionConfig::default();\nlet paths = vec![\"doc1.pdf\", \"doc2.docx\"];\nlet results = batch_extract_file(paths, &config).await?;\n```\n\n### CLI\n```bash\nkreuzberg batch *.pdf --format json\nkreuzberg batch docs/*.docx --output-format markdown\n```\n\n## OCR\n\nOCR runs automatically for images and scanned PDFs. Tesseract is the default backend (native binding, no external install required).\n\n### Backends\n- **Tesseract** (default): Built-in native binding. All Tesseract languages supported.\n- **EasyOCR** (Python only): `pip install kreuzberg[easyocr]`. Pass `easyocr_kwargs={\"gpu\": True}`.\n- **PaddleOCR** (Python only): `pip install kreuzberg[paddleocr]`. Pass `paddleocr_kwargs={\"use_angle_cls\": True}`.\n- **Guten** (Node.js only): Built-in OCR backend via `GutenOcrBackend`.\n\n### Language Codes\n```python\nconfig = ExtractionConfig(ocr=OcrConfig(language=\"eng\"))       # English\nconfig = ExtractionConfig(ocr=OcrConfig(language=\"eng+deu\"))   # Multiple\nconfig = ExtractionConfig(ocr=OcrConfig(language=\"all\"))       # All installed\n```\n\n### Force OCR\n```python\nconfig = ExtractionConfig(force_ocr=True)  # OCR even if text is extractable\n```\n\n## ExtractionResult Fields\n\n| Field | Python | Node.js | Rust | Description |\n|-------|--------|---------|------|-------------|\n| Text content | `result.content` | `result.content` | `result.content` | Extracted text (str/String) |\n| MIME type | `result.mime_type` | `result.mimeType` | `result.mime_type` | Input document MIME type |\n| Metadata | `result.metadata` | `result.metadata` | `result.metadata` | Document metadata (dict/object/HashMap) |\n| Tables | `result.tables` | `result.tables` | `result.tables` | Extracted tables with cells + markdown |\n| Languages | `result.detected_languages` | `result.detectedLanguages` | `result.detected_languages` | Detected languages (if enabled) |\n| Chunks | `result.chunks` | `result.chunks` | `result.chunks` | Text chunks (if chunking enabled) |\n| Images | `result.images` | `result.images` | `result.images` | Extracted images (if enabled) |\n| Elements | `result.elements` | `result.elements` | `result.elements` | Semantic elements (if element_based format) |\n| Pages | `result.pages` | `result.pages` | `result.pages` | Per-page content (if page extraction enabled) |\n| Keywords | `result.keywords` | `result.keywords` | `result.keywords` | Extracted keywords (if enabled) |\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Python\n```python\nfrom kreuzberg import (\n    extract_file_sync, KreuzbergError, ParsingError,\n    OCRError, ValidationError, MissingDependencyError,\n)\n\ntry:\n    result = extract_file_sync(\"file.pdf\")\nexcept ParsingError as e:\n    print(f\"Failed to parse: {e}\")\nexcept OCRError as e:\n    print(f\"OCR failed: {e}\")\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Invalid input: {e}\")\nexcept MissingDependencyError as e:\n    print(f\"Missing dependency: {e}\")\nexcept KreuzbergError as e:\n    print(f\"Extraction failed: {e}\")\n```\n\n### Node.js\n```typescript\nimport {\n    extractFile, KreuzbergError, ParsingError,\n    OcrError, ValidationError, MissingDependencyError,\n} from ''@kreuzberg/node'';\n\ntry {\n    const result = await extractFile(''file.pdf'');\n} catch (e) {\n    if (e instanceof ParsingError) { /* ... */ }\n    else if (e instanceof OcrError) { /* ... */ }\n    else if (e instanceof ValidationError) { /* ... */ }\n    else if (e instanceof KreuzbergError) { /* ... */ }\n}\n```\n\n### Rust\n```rust\nuse kreuzberg::{extract_file, ExtractionConfig, KreuzbergError};\n\nlet config = ExtractionConfig::default();\nmatch extract_file(\"file.pdf\", None, &config).await {\n    Ok(result) => println!(\"{}\", result.content),\n    Err(KreuzbergError::Parsing(msg)) => eprintln!(\"Parse error: {msg}\"),\n    Err(KreuzbergError::Ocr(msg)) => eprintln!(\"OCR error: {msg}\"),\n    Err(e) => eprintln!(\"Error: {e}\"),\n}\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n1. **Python ChunkingConfig fields**: Use `max_chars` and `max_overlap`, NOT `max_characters` or `overlap`.\n2. **Rust extract_file signature**: Third argument is `&ExtractionConfig` (a reference), not `Option`. Use `&ExtractionConfig::default()` for defaults.\n3. **Rust feature gates**: `extract_file_sync`, `batch_extract_file`, and `batch_extract_file_sync` all require `features = [\"tokio-runtime\"]` in Cargo.toml.\n4. **Rust async context**: `extract_file` is async. Use `#[tokio::main]` or call from an async context.\n5. **CLI --format vs --output-format**: `--format` controls CLI output (text/json). `--output-format` controls content format (plain/markdown/djot/html).\n6. **Node.js extractFile signature**: `extractFile(path, mimeType?, config?)` — mimeType is the second arg (pass `null` to skip).\n7. **Python detect_mime_type**: The function for detecting from bytes is `detect_mime_type(data)`. For paths use `detect_mime_type_from_path(path)`.\n8. **Config file field names**: Use snake_case in TOML/YAML/JSON config files (e.g., `max_chars`, `max_overlap`, `pdf_options`).\n\n## Supported Formats (Summary)\n\n| Category | Extensions |\n|----------|-----------|\n| **PDF** | `.pdf` |\n| **Word** | `.docx`, `.odt` |\n| **Spreadsheets** | `.xlsx`, `.xlsm`, `.xlsb`, `.xls`, `.xla`, `.xlam`, `.xltm`, `.ods` |\n| **Presentations** | `.pptx`, `.ppt`, `.ppsx` |\n| **eBooks** | `.epub`, `.fb2` |\n| **Images** | `.png`, `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.gif`, `.webp`, `.bmp`, `.tiff`, `.tif`, `.jp2`, `.jpx`, `.jpm`, `.mj2`, `.jbig2`, `.jb2`, `.pnm`, `.pbm`, `.pgm`, `.ppm`, `.svg` |\n| **Markup** | `.html`, `.htm`, `.xhtml`, `.xml` |\n| **Data** | `.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml`, `.toml`, `.csv`, `.tsv` |\n| **Text** | `.txt`, `.md`, `.markdown`, `.djot`, `.rst`, `.org`, `.rtf` |\n| **Email** | `.eml`, `.msg` |\n| **Archives** | `.zip`, `.tar`, `.tgz`, `.gz`, `.7z` |\n| **Academic** | `.bib`, `.biblatex`, `.ris`, `.nbib`, `.enw`, `.csl`, `.tex`, `.latex`, `.typ`, `.jats`, `.ipynb`, `.docbook`, `.opml`, `.pod`, `.mdoc`, `.troff` |\n\nSee [references/supported-formats.md](references/supported-formats.md) for the complete format reference with MIME types.\n\n## Additional Resources\n\nDetailed reference files for specific topics:\n\n- **[Python API Reference](references/python-api.md)** — All functions, config classes, plugin protocols, exact signatures\n- **[Node.js API Reference](references/nodejs-api.md)** — All functions, TypeScript interfaces, worker pool APIs\n- **[Rust API Reference](references/rust-api.md)** — All functions with feature gates, structs, Cargo.toml examples\n- **[CLI Reference](references/cli-reference.md)** — All commands, flags, config precedence, exit codes\n- **[Configuration Reference](references/configuration.md)** — TOML/YAML/JSON formats, auto-discovery, env vars, full schema\n- **[Supported Formats](references/supported-formats.md)** — All 75+ formats with file extensions and MIME types\n- **[Advanced Features](references/advanced-features.md)** — Plugins, embeddings, MCP server, API server, security limits\n- **[Other Language Bindings](references/other-bindings.md)** — Go, Ruby, Java, C#, PHP, Elixir, WASM, Docker\n\nFull documentation: https://docs.kreuzberg.dev\nGitHub: https://github.com/kreuzberg-dev/kreuzberg\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:08:07.574Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Document Analysis Agents needing advanced text extraction capabilities from 75+ file formats including PDF, Office documents, and images with OCR","zh":"非常适合需要从75+个文件格式（包括PDF、Office文档和带有OCR的图像）中提取高级文本的文档分析代理","ja":"75以上のファイル形式（PDF、Officeドキュメント、OCR付き画像など）から高度なテキスト抽出機能が必要なドキュメント分析エージェントに最適","ko":"75종 이상의 파일 형식(PDF, Office 문서, OCR을 지원하는 이미지 등)에서 고급 텍스트 추출 기능을 필요로 하는 문서 분석 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Documentos que necesitan capacidades de extracción de texto avanzadas de más de 75 formatos de archivo, incluyendo PDF, documentos de Office y imágenes con OCR","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse de Documents ayant besoin de capacités de extraction de texte avancées de plus de 75 formats de fichiers, notamment PDF, documents Office et images avec OCR","de":"Perfekt für Dokumentenanalyse-Agenten, die erweiterte Textextraktionsfunktionen aus über 75 Dateiformaten benötigen, einschließlich PDF, Office-Dokumenten und Bildern mit OCR","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Documentos que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de extração de texto de 75+ formatos de arquivo, incluindo PDF, documentos do Office e imagens com OCR","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа документов, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности извлечения текста из 75+ форматов файлов, включая PDF, документы Office и изображения с OCR","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل المستندات الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لاستخراج النص من 75+ تنسيق ملف ، بما في ذلك PDF ووثائق Office والصور مع OCR"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to extract text, metadata, and structured information from various document formats using a high-performance Rust core, with native bindings for languages like Python, Node.js/TypeScript, and Ruby, and support for protocols like REST API and MCP server","zh":"通过高性能的Rust核心以及对Python、Node.js/TypeScript和Ruby等语言的本地绑定，并支持REST API和MCP服务器等协议，赋予代理从各种文档格式中抽取文本、元数据和结构化信息的能力","ja":"高性能のRustコアと、Python、Node.js/TypeScript、Rubyなどの言語へのネイティブバインディング、またREST APIとMCPサーバーなどのプロトコルに対するサポートにより、エージェントが様々なドキュメント形式からテキスト、メタデータ、構造化情報を抽出する能力を付与する","ko":"고성능의 Rust 코어와 Python, Node.js/TypeScript, Ruby 등 언어에 대한 네이티브 바인딩, 그리고 REST API와 MCP 서버 등을 지원하는 프로토콜을 통해 에이전트가 다양한 문서 형식에서 텍스트, 메타데이터, 구조화된 정보를 추출할 수 있는 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes a extraer texto, metadatos e información estructurada de varios formatos de documento utilizando un núcleo de alto rendimiento en Rust, con enlaces nativos para lenguajes como Python, Node.js/TypeScript y Ruby, y soporte para protocolos como REST API y servidor MCP","fr":"Permet aux agents d''extraire du texte, des métadonnées et des informations structurées de divers formats de documents en utilisant un noyau haute performance en Rust, avec des liaisons natives pour des langages comme Python, Node.js/TypeScript et Ruby, et un support pour des protocoles comme REST API et serveur MCP","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Text, Metadaten und strukturierte Informationen aus verschiedenen Dokumentformaten mithilfe eines hochleistungsfähigen Rust-Kerns zu extrahieren, mit nativen Bindungen für Sprachen wie Python, Node.js/TypeScript und Ruby und Unterstützung für Protokolle wie REST API und MCP-Server","pt":"Habilita os agentes a extrair texto, metadados e informações estruturadas de vários formatos de documento usando um núcleo de alto desempenho em Rust, com vinculações nativas para linguagens como Python, Node.js/TypeScript e Ruby, e suporte a protocolos como REST API e servidor MCP","ru":"Позволяет агентам извлекать текст, метаданные и структурированную информацию из различных форматов документов, используя ядро высокого производительности на Rust, с родными привязками для языков, таких как Python, Node.js/TypeScript и Ruby, и поддержкой протоколов, таких как REST API и сервер MCP","ar":"يسمح للعميل باستخراج النص والبيانات الوصفية والمعلومات المنظمة من تنسيقات وثائق مختلفة باستخدام نواة عالية الأداء في Rust ، مع ربط أصلي للغات مثل Python و Node.js/TypeScript و Ruby ، ودعم بروتوكولات مثل REST API و خادم MCP"},"useCases":{"en":["Extracting text and metadata from PDFs and Office documents","Performing OCR on scanned documents and images","Parsing tables and images from HTML, email, and academic formats"],"zh":["从PDF和Office文档中抽取文本和元数据","对扫描文档和图像执行OCR","从HTML、电子邮件和学术格式中解析表格和图像"],"ja":["PDFとOfficeドキュメントからテキストとメタデータを抽出する","スキャンドキュメントと画像に対してOCRを実行する","HTML、電子メール、学術形式からテーブルと画像を解析する"],"ko":["PDF와 Office 문서에서 텍스트와 메타데이터를 추출","스캔된 문서와 이미지에서 OCR을 수행","HTML, 이메일, 학술 형식에서 표와 이미지를 파싱"],"es":["Extraer texto y metadatos de PDF y documentos de Office","Realizar OCR en documentos y imágenes escaneados","Analizar tablas e imágenes de formatos HTML, correo e