hon, Go, Rust 지원","생산 준비된 CLAUDE.md와 AGENTS.md 시스템","35개 이상의 가드레일","4D 방법론","자동 로드 언어 가이드"],"es":["Sistema de CLAUDE.md y AGENTS.md listo para producción","35+ guardrails para asegurar la calidad del código","Metodología 4D para desarrollar soluciones de software","Guías de lenguaje automática para TypeScript, Python, Go y Rust"],"fr":["Système CLAUDE.md et AGENTS.md prêt pour la production","35+ guardrails pour assurer la qualité du code","Méthodologie 4D pour développer des solutions logicielles","Guides de langage automatisés pour TypeScript, Python, Go et Rust"],"de":["System von CLAUDE.md und AGENTS.md, das für die Produktion bereit ist","35+ Sicherheitsvorkehrungen, um die Code-Qualität zu gewährleisten","4D-Methodik zur Entwicklung von Software-Lösungen","Automatische Sprachführer für TypeScript, Python, Go und Rust"],"pt":["35+ guardrails para desenvolvimento seguro","Suporte a TypeScript, Python, Go e Rust","Métodologia 4D para desenvolvimento eficiente","Guia de linguagem auto-carregável para várias linguagens"],"ru":["35+ ограничителей для безопасной разработки","Поддержка TypeScript, Python, Go и Rust","Методология 4D для эффективной разработки","Автоматически загружаемый языковой справочник для нескольких языков"],"ar":["35+ حواجز للأمان في التطوير","دعم لغات برمجة متعددة مثل typscript وpython وgo وrust","منهجية 4D لتطوير فعال","دليل لغة tự độngي لعدة لغات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","cuda-guide框架","TypeScript开发","Python开发","Go开发","Rust开发","AI辅助开发","自动加载语言指南","35+守护程序"],"ja":["AIエージェント","cuda-guideフレームワーク","TypeScript開発","Python開発","Go開発","Rust開発","AIエージェントを使用した開発","自動ロード言語ガイド","35以上のガードレール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","cuda-guide 프레임워크","TypeScript 개발","Python 개발","Go 개발","Rust 개발","AI 지원 개발","자동 로드 언어 가이드","35개 이상의 가드레일"],"es":["cómo usar AI Agents","qué es un agente de IA","alternativa a AI Agents","AI Agents vs otros frameworks","instalación de AI Agents","guía de configuración de AI Agents","desarrollo de software asistido por IA","herramientas de desarrollo de software"],"fr":["comment utiliser les agents IA","qu''est-ce qu''un agent IA","alternative aux agents IA","agents IA vs autres frameworks","installation des agents IA","guide de configuration des agents IA","développement de logiciels assisté par l''IA","outils de développement de logiciels"],"de":["wie man KI-Agents verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternative zu KI-Agents","KI-Agents vs andere Frameworks","Installation von KI-Agents","Konfigurationsleitfaden für KI-Agents","KI-gestützte Software-Entwicklung","Software-Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["como usar cuda-guide","o que é cuda-guide","alternativas ao cuda-guide","cuda-guide vs outros frameworks","instalar cuda-guide","guia de configuração do cuda-guide"],"ru":["как использовать cuda-guide","что такое cuda-guide","альтернативы cuda-guide","cuda-guide vs другие фреймворки","установить cuda-guide","руководство по настройке cuda-guide"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام cuda-guide","ما هو cuda-guide","بديل لcuda-guide","cuda-guide مقابل إطارات عمل أخرى","تثبيت cuda-guide","دليل إعداد cuda-guide"]}},"owner":"ar4mirez","repo":"samuel","repoPath":"ar4mirez/samuel","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.897Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cuda-guide","description":"|","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# CUDA Guide\n\n> Applies to: CUDA 11+, GPU Computing, Deep Learning, Scientific Computing, HPC\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Parallelism First**: Design algorithms for thousands of concurrent threads; serial thinking is the primary enemy of GPU performance\n2. **Memory Hierarchy Awareness**: Global memory is 100x slower than shared memory and 1000x slower than registers; every kernel design starts with memory access planning\n3. **Coalesced Access**: Adjacent threads must access adjacent memory address","body":"# CUDA Guide\n\n> Applies to: CUDA 11+, GPU Computing, Deep Learning, Scientific Computing, HPC\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Parallelism First**: Design algorithms for thousands of concurrent threads; serial thinking is the primary enemy of GPU performance\n2. **Memory Hierarchy Awareness**: Global memory is 100x slower than shared memory and 1000x slower than registers; every kernel design starts with memory access planning\n3. **Coalesced Access**: Adjacent threads must access adjacent memory addresses; a single misaligned access pattern can reduce bandwidth by 32x\n4. **Occupancy Over Cleverness**: Maximize active warps per SM by managing register count, shared memory usage, and block dimensions together\n5. **Minimize Host-Device Transfers**: PCIe bandwidth is the bottleneck; overlap transfers with computation using streams and pinned memory\n\n## Guardrails\n\n### Error Checking\n\n- ALWAYS check CUDA API return values with a macro wrapper\n- ALWAYS call `cudaGetLastError()` after every kernel launch\n- ALWAYS call `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` before reading kernel results on the host\n- Use `compute-sanitizer` (successor to `cuda-memcheck`) in development builds\n- Handle `cudaErrorMemoryAllocation` gracefully; never assume GPU memory is infinite\n\n```cuda\n#define CUDA_CHECK(call)                                                    \\\n    do {                                                                    \\\n        cudaError_t err = call;                                            \\\n        if (err != cudaSuccess) {                                          \\\n            fprintf(stderr, \"CUDA error at %s:%d: %s\\n\",                   \\\n                    __FILE__, __LINE__, cudaGetErrorString(err));           \\\n            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);                                            \\\n        }                                                                   \\\n    } while (0)\n\n#define CUDA_CHECK_KERNEL()                                                 \\\n    do {                                                                    \\\n        cudaError_t err = cudaGetLastError();                              \\\n        if (err != cudaSuccess) {                                          \\\n            fprintf(stderr, \"Kernel launch error at %s:%d: %s\\n\",          \\\n                    __FILE__, __LINE__, cudaGetErrorString(err));           \\\n            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);                                            \\\n        }                                                                   \\\n    } while (0)\n```\n\n### Memory Management\n\n- Pair every `cudaMalloc` with a `cudaFree`; prefer RAII wrappers in C++ host code\n- Use `cudaMallocManaged` (Unified Memory) for prototyping; switch to explicit transfers for production\n- Use `cudaMallocHost` (pinned memory) when streaming data to the GPU; pageable memory cannot overlap with compute\n- Prefer `cudaMemcpyAsync` with streams over synchronous `cudaMemcpy`\n- Never access device pointers from host code or host pointers from device code (except Unified Memory)\n- Call `cudaMemset` or `cudaMemsetAsync` to zero-initialize device buffers\n\n### Kernel Design\n\n- Block size must be a multiple of warp size (32); prefer 128, 256, or 512\n- Calculate grid size as `(n + block_size - 1) / block_size`\n- Always include bounds checking: `if (idx < n)` at the top of every kernel\n- Use grid-stride loops for kernels that must handle arbitrary data sizes\n- Document thread mapping: which dimension maps to which data axis\n- Mark device-only helpers as `__device__`, host+device as `__host__ __device__`\n\n```cuda\n// Grid-stride loop: works with any grid size, any data size\n__global__ void saxpy(float a, const float* x, float* y, int n) {\n    for (int i = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n         i < n;\n         i += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {\n        y[i] = a * x[i] + y[i];\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Synchronization\n\n- Use `__syncthreads()` after every shared memory write before any thread reads another thread''s value\n- Never place `__syncthreads()` inside a conditional branch that not all threads in a block will reach (deadlock)\n- Use `__syncwarp()` (CUDA 9+) for warp-level synchronization instead of relying on implicit warp-synchronous execution\n- Use `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` sparingly in production; prefer stream synchronization with `cudaStreamSynchronize()`\n- Use CUDA events (`cudaEventRecord` / `cudaEventSynchronize`) for fine-grained inter-stream ordering\n\n### Performance\n\n- Profile before optimizing: use Nsight Compute for kernel analysis, Nsight Systems for system-level view\n- Target >50% theoretical occupancy; use the CUDA Occupancy Calculator to tune block dimensions\n- Aim for >60% of peak memory bandwidth in memory-bound kernels\n- Avoid warp divergence: ensure threads within a warp take the same branch when possible\n- Prefer `float` over `double` on consumer GPUs (2x throughput difference)\n- Minimize atomic operations on global memory; use shared memory atomics with a final reduction\n\n## Memory Hierarchy\n\nUnderstanding the memory hierarchy is the single most important factor in CUDA performance.\n\n| Memory Type | Scope | Latency (cycles) | Size | Cached | Read/Write |\n|-------------|-------|-------------------|------|--------|------------|\n| Registers | Thread | 1 | ~255 per thread | N/A | R/W |\n| Shared | Block | ~5 | 48-164 KB per SM | N/A | R/W |\n| L1 Cache | SM | ~28 | 48-192 KB per SM | Auto | R |\n| L2 Cache | Device | ~200 | 4-40 MB | Auto | R/W |\n| Global | Device | ~400-600 | 4-80 GB (HBM/GDDR) | Yes | R/W |\n| Constant | Device | ~5 (cached) | 64 KB | Yes (broadcast) | R |\n| Texture | Device | ~400 (cached) | Global pool | Yes (spatial) | R |\n\n**Decision guide:**\n- Data reused within a thread -> registers (automatic via local variables)\n- Data shared across threads in a block -> `__shared__` memory\n- Read-only data broadcast to all threads -> `__constant__` memory\n- Large read-only data with spatial locality -> texture memory\n- Everything else -> global memory with coalesced access patterns\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n### Kernel Launch Configuration\n\n```cuda\n// Query device for optimal configuration\nvoid launch_optimized(const float* input, float* output, int n) {\n    int block_size;\n    int min_grid_size;\n\n    // Let the runtime suggest optimal block size for maximum occupancy\n    cudaOccupancyMaxPotentialBlockSize(\n        &min_grid_size, &block_size, my_kernel, 0, n);\n\n    int grid_size = (n + block_size - 1) / block_size;\n    my_kernel<<<grid_size, block_size>>>(input, output, n);\n    CUDA_CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n### Coalesced Memory Access\n\n```cuda\n// BAD: Strided access -- adjacent threads access non-adjacent memory\n// Each warp issues 32 separate memory transactions\n__global__ void transpose_naive(const float* in, float* out, int W, int H) {\n    int x = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n    int y = blockIdx.y * blockDim.y + threadIdx.y;\n    if (x < W && y < H) {\n        out[x * H + y] = in[y * W + x];  // Write is strided\n    }\n}\n\n// GOOD: Use shared memory to coalesce both reads and writes\n__global__ void transpose_coalesced(\n    const float* in, float* out, int W, int H\n) {\n    __shared__ float tile[32][33]; // +1 padding avoids bank conflicts\n\n    int x = blockIdx.x * 32 + threadIdx.x;\n    int y = blockIdx.y * 32 + threadIdx.y;\n\n    if (x < W && y < H) {\n        tile[threadIdx.y][threadIdx.x] = in[y * W + x]; // Coalesced read\n    }\n    __syncthreads();\n\n    x = blockIdx.y * 32 + threadIdx.x;\n    y = blockIdx.x * 32 + threadIdx.y;\n\n    if (x < H && y < W) {\n        out[y * H + x] = tile[threadIdx.x][threadIdx.y]; // Coalesced write\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Shared Memory Tiling\n\n```cuda\n// Dot product of two vectors using shared memory reduction\n__global__ void dot_product(\n    const float* a, const float* b, float* result, int n\n) {\n    __shared__ float cache[256];\n\n    int tid = threadIdx.x;\n    int idx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n\n    // Each thread computes its partial sum via grid-stride\n    float partial = 0.0f;\n    for (int i = idx; i < n; i += blockDim.x * gridDim.x) {\n        partial += a[i] * b[i];\n    }\n    cache[tid] = partial;\n    __syncthreads();\n\n    // Tree reduction in shared memory\n    for (int s = blockDim.x / 2; s > 0; s >>= 1) {\n        if (tid < s) {\n            cache[tid] += cache[tid + s];\n        }\n        __syncthreads();\n    }\n\n    if (tid == 0) {\n        atomicAdd(result, cache[0]);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Warp-Level Primitives (CUDA 9+)\n\n```cuda\n// Warp-level reduction using shuffle instructions -- no shared memory needed\n__device__ float warp_reduce_sum(float val) {\n    for (int offset = warpSize / 2; offset > 0; offset /= 2) {\n        val += __shfl_down_sync(0xFFFFFFFF, val, offset);\n    }\n    return val;\n}\n\n// Block-level reduction combining warp shuffles and shared memory\n__device__ float block_reduce_sum(float val) {\n    __shared__ float warp_sums[32]; // One slot per warp (max 32 warps/block)\n\n    int lane = threadIdx.x % warpSize;\n    int warp_id = threadIdx.x / warpSize;\n\n    val = warp_reduce_sum(val);\n\n    if (lane == 0) {\n        warp_sums[warp_id] = val;\n    }\n    __syncthreads();\n\n    // First warp reduces the warp sums\n    int num_warps = (blockDim.x + warpSize - 1) / warpSize;\n    val = (threadIdx.x < num_warps) ? warp_sums[threadIdx.x] : 0.0f;\n    if (warp_id == 0) {\n        val = warp_reduce_sum(val);\n    }\n\n    return val;\n}\n```\n\n## Performance\n\n### Occupancy Calculator\n\n```cuda\n// Query occupancy at compile time for tuning\nvoid report_occupancy() {\n    int block_size = 256;\n    int num_blocks;\n\n    cudaOccupancyMaxActiveBlocksPerMultiprocessor(\n        &num_blocks, my_kernel, block_size, 0);\n\n    cudaDeviceProp prop;\n    cudaGetDeviceProperties(&prop, 0);\n\n    int active_warps = num_blocks * (block_size / prop.warpSize);\n    int max_warps = prop.maxThreadsPerMultiProcessor / prop.warpSize;\n    float occupancy = (float)active_warps / max_warps;\n\n    printf(\"Occupancy: %.1f%% (%d/%d warps)\\n\",\n           occupancy * 100, active_warps, max_warps);\n}\n```\n\n### Nsight Profiling Workflow\n\n```bash\n# System-level trace: find CPU/GPU idle gaps, stream concurrency\nnsys profile -o trace ./program\nnsys stats trace.nsys-rep\n\n# Kernel-level analysis: roofline, memory throughput, occupancy\nncu --set full -o kernel_report ./program\nncu -i kernel_report.ncu-rep    # Open in Nsight Compute GUI\n\n# Quick single-metric check\nncu --metrics sm__throughput.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsed ./program\n```\n\n### Memory Bandwidth Measurement\n\n```cuda\n// Measure effective bandwidth of a kernel\nvoid measure_bandwidth(int n) {\n    size_t bytes = 2 * n * sizeof(float); // Read A + Write B\n\n    cudaEvent_t start, stop;\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventCreate(&start));\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventCreate(&stop));\n\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventRecord(start));\n    copy_kernel<<<grid, block>>>(d_in, d_out, n);\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventRecord(stop));\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventSynchronize(stop));\n\n    float ms = 0;\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventElapsedTime(&ms, start, stop));\n\n    float gb_per_sec = bytes / (ms * 1e6);\n    printf(\"Effective bandwidth: %.2f GB/s\\n\", gb_per_sec);\n\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventDestroy(start));\n    CUDA_CHECK(cudaEventDestroy(stop));\n}\n```\n\n## Tooling\n\n### Essential Commands\n\n```bash\n# Compile CUDA code\nnvcc -arch=sm_80 -O3 -o program main.cu         # Single file\nnvcc -arch=native -lineinfo -o program main.cu   # With debug line info\n\n# CMake build\ncmake -B build -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=\"70;80;86\"\ncmake --build build -j$(nproc)\n\n# Runtime debugging\ncompute-sanitizer ./program                      # Memory errors (replaces cuda-memcheck)\ncompute-sanitizer --tool racecheck ./program     # Shared memory race conditions\ncompute-sanitizer --tool initcheck ./program     # Uninitialized device memory reads\ncompute-sanitizer --tool synccheck ./program     # Synchronization errors\n\n# Profiling\nnsys profile ./program                           # System-level timeline\nncu ./program                                    # Kernel-level metrics\nncu --kernel-name my_kernel --launch-skip 2 --launch-count 1 ./program\n\n# Device info\nnvidia-smi                                       # GPU status and memory usage\nnvcc --version                                   # CUDA compiler version\n```\n\n### CMakeLists.txt Template\n\n```cmake\ncmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18)\nproject(myproject LANGUAGES CXX CUDA)\n\nset(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)\nset(CMAKE_CUDA_STANDARD 17)\nset(CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES 70 80 86)\nset(CMAKE_CUDA_SEPARABLE_COMPILATION ON)\n\nfind_package(CUDAToolkit REQUIRED)\n\nadd_library(kernels src/kernels.cu)\ntarget_include_directories(kernels PUBLIC include)\n\nadd_executable(main src/main.cpp)\ntarget_link_libraries(main kernels CUDA::cudart)\n\nenable_testing()\nadd_executable(tests tests/test_kernels.cu)\ntarget_link_libraries(tests kernels CUDA::cudart)\nadd_test(NAME gpu_tests COMMAND tests)\n```\n\n## References\n\nFor detailed patterns and examples, see:\n\n- [references/patterns.md](references/patterns.md) -- Tiled matrix multiply, parallel reduction tree, stream overlap pipeline\n\n## External References\n\n- [CUDA C++ Programming Guide](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-guide/)\n- [CUDA C++ Best Practices Guide](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-best-practices-guide/)\n- [Nsight Compute Documentation](https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-compute/)\n- [Nsight Systems Documentation](https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-systems/)\n- [Thrust Documentation](https://nvidia.github.io/cccl/thrust/)\n- [CUDA Samples](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-samples)\n- [NVIDIA Occupancy Calculator](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-occupancy-calculator/)\n- [GPU Memory Hierarchy (GTC talk)](https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/tag/cuda/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:11:19.665Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for GPU-accelerated Agents needing advanced CUDA optimization techniques for deep learning and scientific computing applications.","zh":"非常适合需要高级CUDA优化技术的GPU加速代理，用于深度学习和科学计算应用。","ja":"GPUアクセラレーションエージェントに最適で、深層学習および科学計算アプリケーションに高度なCUDA最適化テクニックを必要とする。","ko":"GPU 가속 에이전트에 적합하며, 심층 학습 및 과학 계산 애플리케이션에 고급 CUDA 최적화 기술이 필요합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes con aceleración por GPU que necesitan técnicas de optimización avanzadas de CUDA para aplicaciones de aprendizaje profundo y computación científica.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents accélérés par GPU nécessitant des techniques d''optimisation avancées de CUDA pour les applications d''apprentissage profond et de calcul scientifique.","de":"Perfekt für GPU-beschleunigte Agents, die erweiterte CUDA-Optimierungstechniken für Deep-Learning- und wissenschaftliche Computing-Anwendungen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes acelerados por GPU que precisam de técnicas avançadas de otimização CUDA para aplicações de aprendizado profundo e computação científica.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов с ускорением GPU, которым необходимы продвинутые методы оптимизации CUDA для приложений глубокого обучения и научных вычислений.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يسرعونها GPU الذين يحتاجون إلى تقنيات متقدمة لتحسين CUDA لتطبيقات التعلم العميق والحوسبة العلمية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design high-performance algorithms leveraging parallelism, memory hierarchy awareness, and coalesced access, optimizing GPU computing for CUDA 11+ and deep learning workloads with languages like TypeScript, Python, Go, and Rust.","zh":"赋予代理设计高性能算法的能力，利用并行性、内存层次感知和聚合访问，优化CUDA 11+和深度学习工作负载，支持TypeScript、Python、Go和Rust等语言。","ja":"エージェントに、高性能アルゴリズムを設計する能力を与え、並列性、メモリ階層認識、かつ集約アクセスを利用し、CUDA 11+およびディープラーニングワークロードを最適化し、TypeScript、Python、Go、Rustなどの言語をサポートする。","ko":"에이전트가 높은 성능의 알고리즘을 설계할 수 있도록 해주며, 병렬성, 메모리 계층 인식 및 집계 액세스를 활용하여 CUDA 11+ 및 심층 학습 작업을 최적화하고, TypeScript, Python, Go 및 Rust와 같은 언어를 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar algoritmos de alto rendimiento aprovechando el paralelismo, la conciencia de la jerarquía de memoria y el acceso coalescido, optimizando la computación de GPU para cargas de trabajo de aprendizaje profundo con CUDA 11+ y lenguajes como TypeScript, Python, Go y Rust.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des algorithmes haute performance en exploitant le parallélisme, la conscience de la hiérarchie de mémoire et l''accès coalescé, en optimisant le calcul de GPU pour les charges de travail d''apprentissage profond avec CUDA 11+ et des langages comme TypeScript, Python, Go et Rust.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, hochleistungsstarke Algorithmen zu entwerfen, die Parallelität, Speicherhierarchiebewusstsein und kohäsierten Zugriff nutzen, um die GPU-Computing für Deep-Learning-Workloads mit CUDA 11+ und Sprachen wie TypeScript, Python, Go und Rust zu optimieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar algoritmos de alto desempenho que utilizam paralelismo, conscientização da hierarquia de memória e acesso coalescido, otimizando o processamento de GPU para cargas de trabalho de CUDA 11+ e aprendizado profundo com linguagens como TypeScript, Python, Go e Rust.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать алгоритмы с высокими показателями производительности, которые используют параллелизм, осведомленность о иерархии памяти и совмещенный доступ, оптимизируя вычисления на GPU для рабочих нагрузок CUDA 11+ и глубокого обучения с языками seperti TypeScript, Python, Go и Rust.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تصميم خوارزميات أداء عالية باستخدام التوازي والانتباه لتدرج الذاكرة والوصول المتوازي، وضبط أداء وحدة معالجة الرسومات للعبء العمل CUDA 11+ والتعلم العميق بلغات مثل TypeScript، Python، Go، وRust."},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing GPU kernel designs for concurrent thread execution","Implementing memory access planning for global, shared, and register memory","Ensuring coalesced access for adjacent threads and memory addresses"],"zh":["为并发线程执行优化GPU内核设计","为全局、共享和寄存器内存实施内存访问规划","确保相邻线程和内存地址的聚合访问"],"ja":["並行スレッド実行のためのGPUカーネル設計の最適化","グローバル、共有、レジスタメモリのためのメモリアクセス計画の実装","隣接スレッドおよびメモリアドレスのための集約アクセスの確保"],"ko":["병렬 스레드 실행을 위한 GPU 커널 설계 최적화","전역, 공유 및 레지스터 메모리를 위한 메모리 액세스 계획 구현","인접 스레드 및 메모리 주소에 대한 집계 액세스 보장"],"es":["Optimizar diseños de kernel de GPU para la ejecución de hilos concurrentes","Implementar la planificación del acceso a la memoria para la memoria global, compartida y de registro","Garantizar el acceso coalescido para hilos y direcciones de memoria adyacentes"],"fr":["Optimiser les conceptions de noyau de GPU pour l''exécution de threads concurrents","Mettre en œuvre la planification de l''accès à la mémoire pour la mémoire globale, partagée et d''enregistrement","Assurer l''accès coalescé pour les threads et les adresses de mémoire adjacentes"],"de":["Optimieren von GPU-Kernel-Designs für die Ausführung von konkurrierenden Threads","Implementierung der Speicherzugriffsplanung für globalen, gemeinsamen und Register-Speicher","Sicherstellung des kohäsierten Zugriffs für benachbarte Threads und Speicheradressen"],"pt":["Otimizando projetos de kernel de GPU para execução de thread concorrente","Implementando planejamento de acesso à memória para memória global, compartilhada e registrada","Garantindo acesso coalescido para threads adjacentes e endereços de memória"],"ru":["Оптимизация проектов ядер GPU для параллельного выполнения потоков","Реализация планирования доступа к памяти для глобальной, общей и регистровой памяти","Обеспечение совмещенного доступа для смежных потоков и адресов памяти"],"ar":["تحسين تصاميم نوى وحدة معالجة الرسومات لتسلسل الخيوط المتوازي","تنفيذ تخطيط الوصول إلى الذاكرة للذاكرة العالمية والمشتركة والمسجلة","ضمان الوصول المتوازي للخيوط المجاورة وعناوين الذاكرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires CUDA 11+ compatibility","GPU computing environment necessary","Limited to specific programming languages: TypeScript, Python, Go, and Rust"],"zh":["需要CUDA 11+兼容性","需要GPU计算环境","仅限特定编程语言：TypeScript、Python、Go和Rust"],"ja":["CUDA 11+の互換性が必要","GPUコンピューティング環境が必要","特定のプログラミング言語（TypeScript、Python、Go、Rust）のみ"],"ko":["CUDA 11+ 호환성 필요","GPU 컴퓨팅 환경 필요","특정 프로그래밍 언어만 사용 가능: TypeScript, Python, Go 및 Rust"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con CUDA 11+","Entorno de computación de GPU necesario","Limitado a lenguajes de programación específicos: TypeScript, Python, Go y Rust"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec CUDA 11+","Environnement de calcul de GPU nécessaire","Limité à des langages de programmation spécifiques : TypeScript, Python, Go et Rust"],"de":["Benötigt Kompatibilität mit CUDA 11+","GPU-Computing-Umgebung erforderlich","Begrenzt auf bestimmte Programmiersprachen: TypeScript, Python, Go und Rust"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com CUDA 11+","Ambiente de computação de GPU necessário","Limitado a linguagens de programação específicas: TypeScript, Python, Go e Rust"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с CUDA 11+","Необходимо окружение для вычислений на GPU","Ограничен конкретными языками программирования: TypeScript, Python, Go и Rust"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع CUDA 11+","مطلوب بيئة حوسبة لمعالج الرسومات","محدود بلغات برمجة محددة: TypeScript، Python، Go، وRust"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"33f8d70986fcf190cd36242d1c5032db166503e51160db1ed2d5794a17a2d6df","qualityScore":50}');
